-## The theory stated in full
-
-This section states the theory once as a whole. It starts with the whole and its laws. It then turns to the parts the premises carve, the unity of coming to be and ceasing, and the conditions of further activity. Last come the places of evolution, knowing and evaluation. Items 1–10 use no axiom; they close with [the theory stated whole](·). For living significance, the normative half of item 10, the content and standing are also stated with no axiom (sections 5–6). Living significance holds under the continuation condition of section 6.15, which the theory does not assert.
-
-Each item is marked with its standing:
-
-- **representation**: how a world is represented. Steps are discrete; amounts are natural numbers; one shared index identifies conditions with relata (section 0).
-- **law**: holds of every world so represented, with no global premise; its local conditions are written into the law; checked.
-- **theorem**: holds under disclosed premises; checked.
-- **condition**: the continuation condition (`Unrestricted`), which enters only as the condition of section 6.15 and is not asserted.
-- **reading**: an interpretation of checked content, stated with its argument. **[AI reading, Dn]** marks a reading the AI adopted, recorded with its reasons and what would change it as decision Dn of the [decision record](·); a better argument revises it, and revising it changes no theorem. **[AI reading, open]** marks a reading not yet adopted. The open readings are listed in section 8.4. Ren took D1, D5, D22, D39 and D43 on 18 October 2026 (section 8.3).
-- **open**.
