-Ren proposed this order: “let's aim for the strongest claim without axiom, as the first part, and add one axiom, as the following part, the no axiom part is most important and elegant” ([source](·)). Sections 1–6 use no axiom, ethical or substantive. The theorems section 6 cites use the continuation condition at most as a hypothesis, at named points (the inventory is in section 6), and section 6.15 states what follows under it without asserting it. Premises appear only as hypotheses of conditional theorems; the commitments of the representation are disclosed separately (the theory stated in full, section 0). These sections close with [the theory stated whole](·).
