-**One unfolding and its readings.** Ren asked of the core's first two layers “is this dualistic?” ([source](·)). They posit no subject and object, but their form takes four splits as given: a configuration and a move drawn from an alphabet of its own; a law prior to the history it governs; claims read off a configuration; and configurations prior to their relations. `World` takes none of them. The four splits are stated here from the world's side, with no premise ([Becoming.Labelled](·), and [Becoming.Unfolding](·) for the readings that also use laws of the world or of the process).
