-**What makes a pair a pair.** Ren asked “what makes a pair, a pair?” ([source](·)). Take a whole of two parts, the combinations that occur. It is rectangular when whatever occurs with one part occurs with every item of the other. Then describing the two parts separately gives the whole back exactly (`separation_faithful_iff`, [Becoming.Description](·)). A whole that is not rectangular is a relation between the parts. Describing them separately loses exactly that relation, and the lost relation reappears as extra combinations (`separation_admits_extra`). Three parts can be related as a whole while every two are free, so describing every pair still loses it (`whole_not_in_pairs`).
