-**Attraction.** The account of a general cause–effect system lists path dependence and attractors. On the spine they are one law, holding of every determined law with no premise ([Becoming.Attraction](·)). A region the law never leaves is absorbing (`Law.Absorbing`). A configuration outside it whose orbit enters it is drawn into it (`Law.DrawnInto`), and what is drawn in is its basin. What is drawn in never comes back (`Law.DrawnInto.never_back`). A configuration is drawn into some absorbing region exactly where it does not return (`Law.drawn_iff_not_returns`): what lies ahead of it is an absorbing region it enters at the first step. The future narrows. What can be had n steps on is an absorbing region, and every possibility lost by step n is drawn into it (`Law.reachable_absorbing`, `Law.lost_drawn`). Of two configurations a law merges, not both return, with no finiteness needed (`Law.Merges.not_both_return`), so not both escape being drawn. Which one is drawn needs deciding, and is stated only in double-negation form (`Law.merge_draws`). Within finitely many configurations, attraction is merging. A drawn configuration means the law merges and loses a possibility; with equality decidable, the two are equivalent; and the region of returning configurations draws in everything else (`Law.Drawn.not_lossless`, `Law.lossless_iff_none_drawn`, `Law.drawnInto_returning`). An open world separates them: counting up draws in without merging, and counting down draws in while keeping every possibility (`Law.succ_drawn_lossless`, `Law.pred_drawn_keeps`). Under every process, once inside an invariant region, configurations outside it can no longer be reached (`Invariant.locks_out`). A region is invariant exactly where every move keeps it, and leaving it needs a move that does not (`invariant_iff_every_move`, `Run.leaving_needs`, `Exit`).
