-**Where a run goes on.** The laws along runs of `Becoming.Branching` take the run as given. Building a run from a configuration that can move takes a continuation at every step, and taking one at every step is a selection the core does not assume. This states where a run goes on with nothing selected, with no premise beyond what each theorem names ([Becoming.Onward](·)). Within finitely many configurations, a course as long as the list repeats a configuration, and the repeated configuration returns. From where a course leads to a return, a run goes round the return, preceded by the course. So a run starts exactly where a course as long as the list starts, exactly where courses of every length start, and exactly where a course leads to a return (`run_iff_continues`, `run_iff_unbounded`, `run_iff_returning`). No decision and no selection are used. Where the successors are listed, whether a run starts is decided (`run_decided`). Where branching is infinite, courses of every length give no run (`fan_no_run`). A family keeps moving where from each member some step leads to a member (`KeepsMoving`). Within finitely many configurations, a run starts at each member and stays in the family (`KeepsMoving.run`). So, within finitely many configurations, the laws along runs hold for every such configuration with no run given. Merging nothing, a configuration returns exactly where a course as long as the list starts from it (`lossless_returns_iff`). Nothing rises within the family, and a rise needs a merge (`lossless_no_rise`, `rise_needs_merge`). A configuration with courses of every length that never returns needs openness (`lossless_unlisted`). Where the configurations are not bounded, consider a test that recognizes, among enumerated moves, a step staying in the family, one wherever there is such a step. It gives a run built by search, as data, with no selection (`Finds`, `search`, `searchedRun`). Where the steps and the family are decided and the steps' moves are enumerated, testing each move is such a test (`decidedTest_finds`). Asked of every process, a run from every member of every family that keeps moving is exactly dependent choice (`runs_iff_selection`, `DependentSelection`). This equivalence is close to definitional, since a run is a dependent-choice sequence; the principle is Bernays's.
