-**The order of change.** Stuttering keeps a world's premises, the totals over stretches and recurrence; rates and reserves counted in steps depend on the reading. Take a given footprint containing the exchanges. Commuting neighbouring exchanges whose footprints are disjoint keeps every premise, and it reaches exactly the renumberings that keep the partial order of joined exchanges (`Footprinted.sorts_iff`, `Footprinted.converse`). Removing idle steps keeps the premises, the censuses and the totals. The footprint is supplied, and removing idle steps uses the moving steps it is given. The least footprint and censuses along reorderings are given in the next paragraph but one, where idleness and apartness are decided. A Foata normal form and continuous time remain open. Records: [only-the-order-of-change-registers](·), [exchanges-commute-unless-joined](·), [order-of-exchanges-is-the-invariant](·). Lean: [Becoming.Order](·). Study: [section 102](·).
