-**Weighted histories and their losses.** Given weights with their laws, and finite lists of moves and configurations, the sum of histories over a finite number of steps is exactly the stepwise transfer (`Weights.sum_courses`). Instances of possibility are the core's traces, and counting keeps possibility. Through a description with representatives, exact preservation at every number of steps is exactly one-step lumpability (`Weights.lumped_iff`). Truncation, cancellation, unkept memory and loops each have explicit boundary witnesses. Not derived: actual weights, amplitudes with phase, convergence of infinite sums, and recovery of memory for general weights. The laws of the weights themselves are explicit structure fields. Records: [sum-over-histories-exact](·), [losses-of-the-sum-over-histories](·). Lean: [Becoming.Weighted](·). Study: [section 104](·).
