-**The exact conditions and boundary of transmission.** Transmission is exactly inheritance with a bound on need (`Flow.transmitsWithin_iff`). Where no dependence was held before, inheritance is the law of forming; the general split into forming and holding uses decidedness. Dropping one dependence of a giver keeps the other premises and breaks binding transmission (`World.drop_but`). Under the named conditions (finiteness, balance, dissipation, embodiment and support), a reading of drawing, with drawing being depending, gives transmission (`World.transmitting_of_drawn`). This does not derive transmission from the other core premises alone. The link is sufficient only; unbounded levels and the formation of new dependences remain open. Records: [transmission-is-inheritance-and-need](·), [transmission-independent-where-it-binds](·). Lean: [Becoming.Transmission](·). Study: [section 105](·).
-
-**Fed without any source recurring.** `Successive.relay` is a balanced, dissipative flow in which only active formations give. Its pool is fed at every step, while each source takes part and is active at its own step only. So continuing to be fed needs no source formation to recur. This advances [continuing-self-fed-from-beyond](·) and is not a separate result. Each source is still needed at its own step. Not shown: that the same world stays fed after a source is removed, and that the sources form from the flow. Lean: [Becoming.Succession](·). Study: [section 106](·).
-
-**The order of exchanges: normal form, census and least footprint.** Take a symmetric joining relation, a finite stretch, and exchanges named by natural numbers. An arrangement is reachable exactly where it orders each joined pair as the original does. Given a decision that distinct exchanges in the stretch are not joined, there is a lexicographically least, idempotent normal form; arrangements are reachable from each other exactly where their normal forms agree. A natural-number-valued complete invariant on a finite stretch needs exactly that decision. Every reordering with its two sides split preserves the existence of activity and standing censuses in both directions; arbitrary commutation preserves it forward. With idleness decided at every step and relatum, there is a least containing footprint, whose joining and order are contained in those of every containing footprint. With equality of relata decidable, a least Boolean containing footprint exists exactly where idleness is decided. The normal form depends on names and on a finite stretch; no unnamed, Foata-layer or unbounded normal form is given. The needed decision is not derived for actual worlds, and no concrete world with undecidable idleness is given. The sides of a reordering remain supplied, and the correspondence with continuous time remains open. [AI reading, D30.] Records: [normal-forms-need-decided-apartness](·), [least-footprint-where-idleness-decided](·); the census result joins [exchanges-commute-unless-joined](·). Lean: [Becoming.OrderNormal](·). Study: [section 109](·).
