-- *Premises carve proper parts.* Seven premises (activity needing support, balance, only active relata giving, only active relata taking what they draw on, dissipation, embodiment, and a reserve carrying activity) are each met by some worlds and not by others. So the premises carve proper parts; they are not hidden laws. The map of premises replaces the reserve with a census and bounded transmission, giving eight independent premises. Which premises follow from which, and the independence of the remaining eight, are in [the map of premises](·) ([map-of-premises](·)).
