-**Feedback and reach.** A formation is affected by another when the other exchanges with a condition it depends on (`Flow.AffectedBy`). The following states, with no axiom, how far a formation's own feedback reaches, how far a part's exchange reaches, and where the comparison with and without a part is decided ([Becoming.Feedback](·)). The formalization and the names are the AI's.
-
-- **Five levels** ([levels-of-closure](·)). A region is closed under a relation when whatever a member bears the relation to is a member, and a formation lies within another's closure when every closed region holding the other holds it (`ClosedUnder`, `WithinClosure`); this is the seed–edge closure from one seed (`withinClosure_iff_closure`, `Becoming.EdgeClosure`). The feeding closure is the closure under being fed (`Flow.withinFeeding_iff`). The closure under being affected is the influence closure, what can affect the formation (`Flow.WithinInfluence`); the closure under affecting is the reach closure, what the formation's exchange can affect, link by link (`Flow.Affects`, `Flow.WithinReach`). Two formations share a condition when both take part in it, by depending on it or exchanging with it (`Flow.Shares`), and the closure under sharing is the system, a class (`Flow.WithinSystem`, `Flow.WithinSystem.symm`). Each formation lies within its feeding closure, which lies within its influence closure; the influence and reach closures lie within the system (`Flow.withinInfluence_of_withinFeeding`, `Flow.withinSystem_of_withinInfluence`, `Flow.withinSystem_of_withinReach`). Each inclusion can be strict, and the influence and reach closures point in opposite directions. In `Clearing` the source lies within the clearer's feeding closure and beyond its reach closure, and the dweller beyond its influence closure and within its reach closure (`Clearing.levels`, `Clearing.reach_middle`); the dweller's reach closure holds only the dweller (`Clearing.reach_centred`). `Trophic` is a trophic cascade: wolves lie beyond a forest's feeding closure and within its influence closure, affecting it through the deer, and a formation far off lies beyond the forest's system (`Trophic.mediates`).
-- **One common condition makes the system the whole.** Where every formation takes part in one condition, every system is the whole (`Flow.system_whole_of_common`), as in `Clearing` (`Clearing.clearer_system`, `Clearing.system_whole`). Formations that depend on one condition share a system even where nothing exchanges with it and neither affects the other (`Static.shares_unaffected`). Where every formation depends on one condition and exchanges with it, every reach closure is the whole (`Flow.reach_whole_of_common`). Where at one step every formation requires one condition and gives to it, every feeding closure is the whole, and significance bounded by it, the route without axiom of `Becoming.Interdependence`, is the condition (`Flow.feeding_whole_of_common`, `Flow.feeding_unrestricted_of_common`).
-- **Levels follow their exchanges.** Two balanced flows that start a condition alike, and take from it and give to it alike, keep it alike (`Flow.Balances.levels_agree`). So a formation's support registers only the exchanges with what it depends on (`Flow.Balances.support_agrees`). What a part does registers on a condition exactly through its net exchange with it (`Flow.Balances.agrees_iff_even`). The levels with and without the part agree where none of its members exchanges with the condition (`Flow.Balances.agrees_of_quiet`); where they differ at a step, some member exchanged with it at an earlier step (`Flow.Balances.exchanges_before_of_differs`).
-- **What feedback registers** ([feedback-and-reach](·)). Nothing beyond a formation's influence closure exchanges with a condition that a member of the closure depends on (`Flow.beyond_influence`). Where every member of a part lies beyond the closure, each formation within it is supported with the part exactly where the levels without the part admit it (`Flow.Balances.uncoupled_beyond_influence`). In `Clearing` the clearer's support is the same at every step whether or not it clears the habitat, while the dweller ends (`Clearing.uncoupled`). The influence closure is an upper bound: with the rest of the exchange fixed, a formation's support registers only the parts that reach it directly (`Flow.Balances.admits_unreached`).
-- **What a part reaches.** A part reaches a formation when a member exchanges with a condition the formation depends on (`Flow.Reaches`), and reaches it before a step when a member exchanged, at an earlier step, with a condition the formation requires at that step (`Flow.ReachesBefore`). Whatever a part has not reached before a step is admitted alike with and without it there (`Flow.Balances.admits_unreached_before`, `Flow.Balances.admits_unreached`). An exchange that comes after the dependence affects without effect (`Late.affected_without_effect`). What a part whose members lie within a region closed under affecting reaches lies within the region (`Flow.reaches_within_closed`); the reach closure and the system are such regions (`Flow.reaches_withinReach`, `Flow.withinSystem_closed`), and a formation's own part has its members within its reach closure (`Flow.own_within_reach`). What lies within a system reaches only within it, and what lies beyond reaches nothing within it (`Flow.reaches_withinSystem`, `Flow.unreached_within_system`).
-- **The comparison is decided within what the part reaches** ([comparison-within-reach](·)). Two significances that agree, from a standpoint, at each step on what the part has reached before it compare the levels with and without the part alike (`Flow.Balances.comparison_local`). For any significance that covers what the part has reached before each step, the levels with and without the part retain what has significance along each other exactly as they include each other, both ways, and neither adds a continuation with significance exactly where neither exceeds the other: the condition's comparisons (`Flow.Balances.comparison_within_reach`). Where significance is decidable, adding is exceeding (`Flow.Balances.adds_iff_exceeds_of_decidable`). So significance bounded by a region closed under affecting compares every part within it as inclusion does (`Flow.Balances.closed_comparison`), and the reach closure is the least such region holding a center. In `Clearing` the clearer's part reaches the dweller (`Clearing.reaches_dweller`). Significance bounded by each reach closure is not the condition, yet from the clearer's standpoint the part loses the dweller, as under the condition (`Clearing.reach_counts_dweller`); bounded by each influence closure, the part retains (`Clearing.system_counts_dweller`).
-- **Any two flows.** The comparison of any two balanced flows that start alike is decided within what their difference reaches before each step (`Flow.DiffersBefore`, `Flow.Balances.comparison_within_difference`). With the rest of the exchange fixed the difference is a part's exchange; where others respond, it holds their responses as well. The wolves' part does not reach the forest, while the difference from the flow in which the deer respond reaches it (`Trophic.difference_reaches_forest`).
-- **Where the comparison stops.** Covering is enough and not needed: a part can reach beyond a formation's influence closure and change no admission there (`Margin.reach_without_misjudgment`). A part with a member beyond a system can be misjudged by significance bounded by that system (`Trophic.mixed_part`). The comparison by withheld levels holds the rest of the exchange fixed, so effects through others' responses do not register in it: with the deer's browsing held as it is, the wolves' part narrows, closing the deer (`Trophic.mediated_uncoupled`); against the flow in which the deer respond, the same taking is mixed (`Trophic.responsive_mixed`). Where a part gives what others take, the levels without it may not exist, and there is no comparison by withheld levels (`Clearing.no_levels_without_source`).
-
-Feedback and a part's exchange point in opposite directions: a formation's feedback registers at most its influence closure, what can affect it, while its own part reaches into its reach closure, what it can affect. Whether a formation knows beyond its feedback, the dynamics do not decide. The comparison by withheld levels keeps the rest of the exchange fixed, and a part is a decided family of formations, so one act of a formation is not separated from its other exchanges and is compared through a second flow, as in `Clearing.uncoupled`; the representation commits to discrete steps and natural-number amounts. Readings of reach, the system one is in and situational awareness are the AI's [AI reading, D20].
-
-**The comparison where the rest responds.** The comparison by withheld levels keeps the rest of the exchange fixed, and the comparison of any two flows is decided within what their difference reaches, without saying where that difference can go. This module states where it can go when the rest responds through what it registers ([Becoming.Response](·)). A formation lies within a part's responsive reach when it lies within some member's closure under affecting through what is registered: a member exchanges, in one of the two flows, with a condition the formation registers, or reaches it by such links (`Flow.WithinResponse`). The rest responds through its registration when every formation outside the part exchanges alike in the two flows across each step up to which it has registered alike (`Flow.RespondsThroughCoupling`); this is a supplied premise, not derived from the dynamics, and the rest held fixed is a case of it (`Flow.respondsThroughCoupling_withhold`). Under it, with the same formations present, balance and a common start on what the formations beyond the responsive reach register, each of them registers alike and exchanges alike at every step (`Flow.alike_beyond_response`, an instance of `Flow.alike_within_closed`), and the difference between the flows reaches none of them (`Flow.not_differs_beyond_response`). So for two balanced flows starting alike, any significance covering every formation not beyond the responsive reach compares them as the condition does (`Flow.Balances.comparison_within_response`). The responsive reach is the dual of the registration closure (`Flow.withinResponse_iff_coupling`) and holds what the part reaches and each member's reach closure; registering support only, with one flow, it is exactly the union of the members' reach closures (`Flow.withinResponse_thresholdOnly_iff`). In the trophic cascade the deer respond through their support: the forest lies within the wolves' responsive reach, which their part does not reach, and the reach is exactly the wolves, the deer and the forest, among which the responsive comparison is decided (`Trophic.within_response_iff`, `Trophic.responsive_comparison`). In `Loop` a part's act changes what another formation registers, the other responds, and the difference returns to the part's own support, which the part's own exchange never reaches (`Loop.returns`). *Readings* [AI reading, D25]. An act has two counterfactuals: with the rest fixed only what the part reaches directly counts, and with the rest responding through its registration the responsive reach counts; an escalation loop is the case where each party responds through its registration and the difference returns to the part; registering support only, the reach closure is where the difference an act makes can arrive when the rest responds through its support. That formations respond only through their registration and how they respond are not derived; how much difference arrives is answered in `Becoming.Propagation` where the rest follows a law with given coupling strengths. Record: [comparison-where-the-rest-responds](·). Study: [section 87](·).
-
-**The response as the dynamics give.** The comparison of `Becoming.Response` supplies two things: the second flow, and the premise that the rest responds through its registration. This module gives the rest's exchange as a law and derives both ([Becoming.Counterfactual](·)). A law of exchange reads off a level history what each formation takes from and gives to each condition at each step (`ExchangeLaw`); it reads what has stood when, across the step from `t`, it reads the history up to `t` only (`ExchangeLaw.Nonanticipating`). Two balanced flows with the same formations present, starting alike, in which the part acts alike and the rest follows one law of what has stood, have the same levels and the same exchange at every step (`counterfactual_fixed`): once the law is given, the course of an act is not supplied. The law generates a course step by step from starting levels, the orbit of one determined law on the stage and the history so far (`ExchangeLaw.history_orbit`), and the generated flow balances exactly where the law never takes more from a condition than stands on it and is given to it (`ExchangeLaw.course_balances_iff`). So the counterfactual of an act is the course it generates (`counterfactual_is_course`), and where every formation follows one law of what has stood, a balanced flow is the course the law generates (`ExchangeLaw.course_unique`). Where the law reads, for each formation outside the part, only what it registers (`ExchangeLaw.Through`), the rest responds through its registration in any two courses of the law (`ExchangeLaw.Through.responds`): the premise of `Becoming.Response` becomes a theorem. Every law of what has stood reads through registering everything; with finitely many conditions it reads through the conditions its exchange is sensitive to (`ExchangeLaw.Nonanticipating.through_sensitive`), and no registration it reads through, with what the formation depends on, leaves out a condition it is sensitive to (`ExchangeLaw.Through.couples_of_sensitive`, in double-negation form: it cannot fail to hold such a condition): sensitivity is the least registration, at that strength. So the comparison of two courses of the law is decided within the responsive reach drawn through the law's registration, which with finitely many conditions is its sensitivity; and so is the comparison of an act with the course another act generates, with neither the second flow nor the response supplied (`comparison_of_courses`, `comparison_through_sensitivity`, `comparison_with_act`). The act is the input of a standard causal model: the course is a trajectory of the model of `Becoming.Mechanism` whose input is the part's move, and an act not taken is an intervention, whose outcome the record does not fix and the model does (`ExchangeLaw.course_trajectory`, `ExchangeLaw.act_not_taken`). In the `Loop` of `Becoming.Response` the second's reply is a law reading only what it observes, `Loop.responds` follows from it, and each flow is the only balanced course of the law with its act (`Loop.responds_by_law`, `Loop.courses_fixed`). As an unfolding of `Becoming.Unfolding`: where formations and conditions are one kind of relatum, the course is a world running by the law of exchange exactly where feasible (`ExchangeLaw.world_exchange_iff`); a determined law steps beyond what a run of it shows exactly at the moves the run never takes (`Run.beyond_shown_iff`, a law about `Shown`), so what lies beyond the course's history is exactly its counterfactuals (`ExchangeLaw.counterfactual_beyond_shown`); with the part's move formed by a law on the configuration, a run of `closedBy` is the course (`ExchangeLaw.closedBy_course`). *Readings* [AI reading, D25]. A counterfactual is not a second world beside the actual one but the course of the same law with the part acting otherwise, existing where feasible and fixed by the act, the law's step beyond its history rather than a second history beside it; for a rest following a law of what has stood, the premise of `Becoming.Response` is no further assumption about how formations behave, and, read as 识 (shí, registering), a formation registers what its exchange is sensitive to. The law itself, that it reads what has stood, and feasibility are not derived. Whether sensitivity is still the least registration with infinitely many conditions is answered in `Becoming.Sensitivity`: it is wherever the law reads finitely many conditions under each history; whether that condition can be dropped turns on omniscience: given a decision of whether levels vanish eventually the tail law is a counterexample, and with the conditions numbered every counterexample gives the weak limited principle of omniscience; a counterexample exists exactly where a rule decides, of every Boolean sequence, whether it is false throughout (`Becoming.Tail`). When a move is the part's own is answered in `Becoming.Coupling`: exactly where it is formed through the part's configuration. Records: [counterfactual-is-the-course](·), [comparison-where-the-rest-responds](·). Study: [section 100](·).
-
-**What a law of the whole and no part takes.** `Becoming.Sensitivity` leaves open the exact strength of the existence of a counterexample, between the weak limited principle of omniscience and the decision of vanishing ([Becoming.Tail](·)). A number read off levels is changed by no condition where levels differing at one condition only give it alike (`ChangedByNoCondition`); exactly then levels agreeing from some condition on give it alike, the conditions below being changed one at a time (`ChangedByNoCondition.eq_of_agree_from`, `ChangedByNoCondition.of_agree_from`): what no part changes, only the tail sets. The law of the whole exchanging such a number (`wholeLaw`) reads what has stood, is insensitive at every step to every condition and reads through the conditions from any one on; where the number differs, it does not read through what it is sensitive to, nor finitely many conditions, and the registrations it reads through have no least one (`wholeLaw_not_through_sensitive`, `wholeLaw_not_readsFinitely`, `wholeLaw_no_least_coupling`); the tail law is the instance of the indicator of vanishing (`tailLaw_eq_wholeLaw`). `Becoming.Sensitivity` mixes two histories along a Boolean sequence and then compares two numbers; comparing numbers is decided, so every counterexample gives not only the weak limited principle of omniscience but a rule deciding, of every Boolean sequence, whether it is false throughout (`mixedDecision`, `insensitiveDiffersDecision`, `notThroughSensitiveDecision`; the rule gives `WLPO`, `WLPO.of_rule`). Conversely, given such a rule, whether levels vanish from condition N on is decided (`vanishesFrom`), and whether they vanish from no condition on is decided by the rule again (`neverIndicator`, `vanishesFrom_never_iff`); this indicator is changed by no condition, tells levels all 0 from levels all 1, and with the decision of vanishing given sums with the indicator of vanishing to 1 (`neverIndicator_add_vanishIndicator`); its law is a counterexample built from the rule alone (`neverLaw`). So a number changed by no condition that still differs, a law insensitive at a step to every condition that still differs there, and a counterexample to the least registration each exist exactly where such a rule does (`changedByNoCondition_iff_rule`, `insensitive_differs_iff_rule`, `not_through_sensitive_iff_rule`). The decision of vanishing is exactly the limited principle of omniscience as a rule: it decides of every Boolean sequence whether it has a true, and such a rule decides vanishing in two passes (`lpoRuleOfVanishDecision`, `vanishDecisionOfLPORule`, `vanishDecision_iff_lpoRule`), giving the weak rule and `LPO` (`wlpoRuleOfLPORule`, `LPO.of_rule`); so the tail law takes the limited principle as a rule, where a counterexample needs only the weak one. *Readings* [AI reading, D43]. What depends on the whole and on no part of it is given exactly where it can be decided, of every unending record of yes and no, whether it says no throughout; with the conditions numbered, the least registration fails exactly at this omniscience and needs no more of it, and the core does not assume it; read as whether levels never vanish, a whole of this kind takes only the weak rule, and read as whether they vanish eventually, a related whole, classically its complement but in the core another law, takes the rule of the limited principle. Whether the proposition `WLPO` gives a rule (choosing a function from a relation, which the core does not assume), whether the weak rule gives the limited principle, and what a counterexample gives where the conditions are not numbered by the natural numbers are not derived. See [what-a-law-of-the-whole-and-no-part-takes](·).
