-**How much difference arrives.** The responsive reach says where a difference can go, and sensitivity whether a level can change an exchange; neither says how much ([Becoming.Propagation](·)). Across a step the difference of two levels (`gap`, what either has beyond the other) changes by exactly the difference given less the difference taken: in two balanced flows, the first's level of a condition after the step and the second's before, with what the first takes and the second gives, equal the second's level after and the first's before, with what the second takes and the first gives (`levels_step_exact`). So a condition's gap across a step is at most its gap before with the gaps of every exchange with it (`gap_step`), and does not grow where every exchange is alike (`gap_step_of_alike`). A formation's exchange with a condition is coupled to the level of a condition at a step with strength at most k where, under any two histories differing in that level only, what it takes and gives differ in all by at most k times that level's gap (`ExchangeLaw.RespondsWithin`): the measure of sensitivity. For a law of what has stood, strength zero is insensitivity (`ExchangeLaw.insensitiveAt_iff_strength_zero`, `ExchangeLaw.sensitive_iff_strength`); strengths add up over levels changed one at a time (`ExchangeLaw.exchangeGap_le_mixCells`, `ExchangeLaw.exchangeGap_le_strengths`), so the change of a move is at most the part's share, its strengths times the part's change, with the rest's share (`ExchangeLaw.exchangeGap_le_shares`). A finite strength is a condition on a law, not given with every law: a law giving the square of a level has none (`Propagation.Square.not_respondsWithin`). The carrying law has the part give its gaps and each formation outside it give what its strengths make of the levels so far, taking nothing (`ExchangeLaw.carrying`); the carried amount is the course it generates from the starting gaps (`carried`, by `Becoming.Counterfactual`'s generation). Where the rest follows in both flows one law of what has stood with those strengths, the part differing by at most its gaps and the starting levels by at most theirs, every gap at every step is at most the carried amount (`gap_le_carried`). It is attained: the carrying law has those strengths, and its course differs from the quiet course by exactly the carried amount (`ExchangeLaw.carrying_respondsWithin`, `carried_attained`), so the carried amount is the most difference that can arrive (`most_difference_arrives`, an equivalence). It is positive exactly along a route in time of positive strengths (`Conveyed`, `carried_pos_iff`); where there is none the two flows' levels agree (`levels_alike_of_not_conveyed`), and where the positive strengths are registered the routes are those of `TimedResponse`'s spread (`Conveyed.spread`). Carried differences add (`carried_add`), and more gaps and larger strengths carry more (`carried_mono`). Witnesses: one unit given once, which the rest relays each step to a second condition at twice its level, arrives there as 2t by step t + 1, without bound and with no loop (`Propagation.Chain.keeps_arriving`); returned by a loop of strength one, it arrives as 2^t (`Propagation.Loop.runaway`). *Readings* [AI reading, D39]. The coupling strength is the measure sensitivity lacked, sensitivity saying whether and the strength how strongly; how much difference arrives is itself a course, generated by one law and read off the unfolding rather than added to it; a held difference keeps arriving, since levels hold what they are given, under a law that takes nothing and so creates amounts (the carrying law); under the first law this is not shown, and in a finite whole whose rest gives nothing net the levels stay within the stock (`Flow.whole_bounded_of_rest_idle`). The strengths themselves are supplied bounds, and no least strength is stated; infinitely many conditions, continuous time and real amounts are not derived; a general theory of loops is given in `Becoming.Loops`. See [how-much-difference-arrives](·).
