-**The orders of a carried difference as a sum over histories.** Ren took the reading that the integration asked about on 12 October is the sum over histories of `Becoming.Weighted` with its losses, that the orders of `Becoming.Loops` are of the same structural kind, and that the two were not yet joined ([Becoming.Routes](·)). For every weighting, each step's weight split into a ground and a response part, order j (`Weights.within`) reads order j through the ground part and order j − 1 through the response part, and is the whole sum over histories at every horizon up to j (`Weights.within_exact`); with one configuration, ground one and response M, order j is `Loops.orderSum M j n` and the sum (1 + M)^n (`Routes.SelfLoop.within_eq`, `Routes.SelfLoop.transfer_eq`). Traced back in time, a difference steps by one response to an earlier level, weighted by the strengths summed over the steps at which it can occur with the level holding between (`responseWeight`), or ends at a source (`routeWeight`). The transfer of these counting weights at horizon j + 1 is order j of the carried amount (`routeSum_eq_carriedWithin`), so each order and the carried amount are sums over courses (`carriedWithin_eq_courses`, `carried_eq_courses`), a cut is a truncation (`routeSum_exact`, `carried_le_routeSum_add`), and with the same formations and strengths at every step a finite horizon is exact exactly where no loop lies upstream (`finite_horizon_iff_no_loop`). *Readings* (the AI's, agreed by Ren on 16 October 2026; [source](·)). The two integrations are one, the responses being the vertices of a diagram and the level holding between them as a propagator sums over intermediate times; the loss by loops of `Becoming.Weighted` is the runaway of `Becoming.Loops`; the match is structural, and counting weights do not cancel.
