-**How loops form within the unfolding.** Ren took the reading that loops form and dissolve within the unfolding, pending a loop-formation theorem ([Becoming.Closing](·)). The strengths before step T (`strengthsBefore`) keep the couplings acting before T (`couples_before_iff`), so the loops formed by T are stated with the definitions of `Becoming.Loops`; every chain is formed by some step, and a world's loops are exactly those formed by some step (`onLoop_iff_formed`). A loop forms by closing: the loops formed by T + 1 are those formed by T and those through a coupling acting at step T that closes a chain (`onLoop_succ_iff`, `forms_by_closing`); an exchange coming to respond to the level of the condition it gives to forms a loop of one (`responds_to_own_level`). The carried amount up to T reads only the couplings before T (`carried_before`), so with no loop formed by T upstream it is at most a polynomial up to T (`carried_le_polynomial_before`); the amounts before a loop forms do not show whether it will (`Closing.Onset`). Where strengths are read from the levels up to each step (`ReadsBefore`), the course generated is the carried amount of the strengths it reads (`formedCourse_eq_carried`): formation is read off the unfolding; in the threshold witness the loop forms at the step a level reaches the threshold and doubles from then on (`Closing.Threshold`). How loops dissolve is in `Becoming.Remainder` (couplings that stop). *Readings* (the AI's, agreed by Ren on 16 October 2026). A loop forms by closing, at the step an exchange comes to respond to a level downstream of what it gives to; its formation is not foreseen from the amounts before it, which meets `Becoming.Runaway`.
-
-**Loops within what a law reads, and the break.** The reading Ren took left open “where a formation's drawing comes to respond to the level its drawing lowers, where this meets `Becoming.Runaway`”, and Ren asked for the two to be joined ([Becoming.Thresholds](·)). A law reads a schedule (`ExchangeLaw.ReadsAt`) when, for each formation outside the part, it gives alike under histories agreeing on the conditions the schedule marks. An unread level is coupled with strength zero (`ExchangeLaw.ReadsAt.respondsWithin_unread`), so the strengths restricted to what is read are strengths of the law (`ExchangeLaw.ReadsAt.restrict`); a law reading through a registration reads every schedule covering it (`ExchangeLaw.Through.readsAt`), and its courses are policies through registration in the sense of `Becoming.Runaway` (`ExchangeLaw.Through.policyThrough`). So loops lie within what is read: every coupling reads its level (`couples_reads`), a draw responds to the level it lowers only where it reads it (`self_coupling_reads`), no loop passes through a level nothing reads (`not_onLoop_unread`), and a loop forms at a step only through a formation reading there a level downstream of where it gives (`onLoop_succ_reads`). For every law, two courses apart only in a stock nothing reads are alike everywhere else, the stock's gap held (`unread_carried_nowhere`). A law reads a stock only below a threshold (`ExchangeLaw.ReadsBelow`) when, while the stock stands at the threshold, it reads only that it stands; every law reading through a registration in which no formation outside the part observes the stock, with the threshold at least each need of it, is such a law (`ExchangeLaw.Through.readsBelow`), so `Becoming.Runaway`'s formation is an instance. For every such law, raising the stock by any amount changes nothing else up to the break (`break_carried_nowhere`): the distance to the break is carried nowhere, for the whole law and not only for one policy with the rest fixed. Before the break the law is its standing law (`ExchangeLaw.standing`, `Flow.follows_standing_before`), which does not read the stock, is coupled to it with strength zero and has no loop through it (`ExchangeLaw.ReadsBelow.standing_no_loop`): the loop through the stock forms at the break. Witness (`Thresholds.Draw`): a formation draws one unit from a stock and gives it to a product at each step while the stock stands at N + 1; every strengths of it couple the stock into itself, a loop of one (`Draw.onLoop`), yet before the break it gives as its standing law (`Draw.forms_at_break`); at a step where one course's stock stands below the threshold and a raised one's at it, the raised course gives one more to the product (`Draw.diverges_at_break`). *Readings* (the AI's, agreed by Ren on 16 October 2026). A runaway's break is where a loop forms; the blindness of `Becoming.Runaway` and the formation of `Becoming.Closing` are one event seen from two sides; what can register how near the break is, is a reading of the stock's level before it. See [loops-within-what-a-law-reads](·).
