-**How often couplings act: settling, runaway and its rate.** `Becoming.Remainder` leaves three questions: whether every schedule of couplings settles, whether every loop of recurring couplings makes the most difference that can arrive run away, and how fast a runaway is ([Becoming.Frequency](·)). A schedule (`on`) marks steps, and `Frequency.count` counts those before step t. With the part giving no gap after the start, starting gaps at most D, and the strengths into each condition at most M at each step and zero at unmarked steps, the carried amount at step t is at most D·(1 + M)^a, a the marked steps before it (`carried_le_count`): the geometric bound of `Becoming.Loops` multiplies only at marked steps; with every condition listed, the steps at which anything couples are such a schedule (`Frequency.coupling`, `carried_le_coupling`). One condition returning its level to itself with strength M at the steps of any schedule couples exactly there (`Frequency.SelfLoop.couplesAt_iff`) and carries exactly D·(1 + M)^a (`Frequency.SelfLoop.carried_eq`): no smaller bound follows from D, M and the steps at which couplings act; by `most_difference_arrives` the rate bounds the gaps of every law with the strengths (`gap_le_count`). A coupling reading an earlier level adds, across its step, at least what had reached that level (`carried_step_ge_at`); a chain in time order carries what reached its start to its end (`ChainInTime`, `carried_along_in_time`), and a return (`Returns`) is such a chain from a condition back to it. Every return at least doubles what had reached the condition, which arrives once held and once around the loop; strengths are natural numbers, so a positive strength is at least one (`carried_doubles_return`), and R returns multiply it by 2^R (`carried_returns`); so where something has arrived and returns come at steps T i with 2^i outgrowing every polynomial in T i, the most difference that can arrive outgrows every polynomial, whatever the strengths (`runaway_of_returns`). Conversely, where 2^a is bounded by a polynomial so is the carried amount, whatever the strengths (`carried_le_of_rare`); for a self-loop the two meet: it is polynomial exactly where 2^a is (`Frequency.SelfLoop.polynomial_iff`). The sparse schedule marks the steps one less than a power of two, 0, 1, 3, 7, … (`Frequency.Sparse`): the self-loop coupling there recurs, so every finite order misses something (`Frequency.Sparse.inexact`), yet it carries at most D·2^M·(t + 1)^M (`Frequency.Sparse.polynomial`): a loop of recurring couplings need not run away. A coupling that stops by step N (`StopsBy`) does not recur; with every condition listed, where each coupling recurs or stops, the schedule has settled by some step (`settled_of_each`): settling is local. Whether a coupling at step m reads a level from step n on is decided (`Frequency.readsLate`), so given the dichotomy that every decided two-place family has every row true somewhere or some row false throughout (`RecursOrStops`), every schedule settles (`settled_of_recursOrStops`); conversely, every schedule of one condition returning to itself settles exactly where the dichotomy holds (`settled_iff_recursOrStops`), and so for every world with its conditions listed (`settled_every_iff`). The self-loop coupling at the first step a decided sequence is true couples at most once (`Frequency.First.once`), and these schedules all settling gives the limited principle of omniscience (`lpo_of_settled`); the self-loop reading level s once every row up to s has been true somewhere recurs exactly where every row is (`Frequency.Rows.recurs_iff`). The self-loop of `Becoming.Loops` and the loop of `Becoming.Closing` forming at T are instances (`Frequency.SelfLoop.always_carried`, `Frequency.SelfLoop.onset_amount`). *Readings* [AI reading, D43]. Ren asked on 12 October 2026 “how how accurate can we do that uh what is the limitation do we have losses” ([source](·)); how fast a difference runs away is set by how often couplings act: with natural-number strengths, each positive one at least one, frequent returns make it run away (with strengths below one they need not), and rare coupling steps keep it polynomial whatever the strengths, strength changing only how large; for a self-loop, how often it couples decides exactly. On 16 October Ren called the AI's reading of “only a loop makes a difference run away” right, a reading that left couplings at only some steps open ([source](·)); that case is now closed both ways: only a loop of the couplings that go on can make it run away, and such a loop need not. That every schedule settles is a principle of reasoning, not a fact the theory asserts or denies of the unfolding; the theorems write a settled schedule in as a premise where they need one. Not derived: which of the bound by returns and the bound by coupling steps is met beyond the self-loop, the spectral radius of given strengths, real amounts (a positive strength may be below one, and strengths shrinking fast enough could keep frequent returns from running away), laws reading infinitely many conditions at a step, and continuous time. See [how-often-couplings-act](·).
-**Continuity across dormancy, and identity fixed by relations.** First read which relations of the same unfolding still hold across an inactive step. Given a reading of holding `h`, `Web.persisting h` reads activity by it. A formation that wakes having held before does not arise under this reading. Where the names of what holds continue step by step, there is one name over each held stretch, and the renewing or consuming class of a formation that holds throughout does not change (`Web.steady_held`, `Web.renewingIn_held`, `Web.consumingIn_held`). This is stronger than the earlier two-way continuity of activity and tenure (`Hibernation.readings`), and still does not constrain succession at a step where nothing holds (`Dormancy.held_both`). Dependence and reserve give a seed different readings of its ending (`Seed.held_readings`). Both ends of a census must read holding alike; mixing the readings can fail (`Web.persisting_census`, `Sleeper.held_readings`).
-
-A re-identification of a world keeps balance exactly where what it continues at each step lies within the conservation relation `World.Conserves` (`World.balanced_reidentify_iff`, with no further hypothesis). In a balanced world this is equality of the amounts standing after the step, which is likeness of the exchange frames (`World.balanced_reidentify_iff_alike`). With equality of relata decidable, the exact conditions under which identity, arising and ceasing are fixed under every naming that keeps balance are given by `World.fixed_iff`, `World.arises_fixed_iff` and `World.ceases_fixed_iff`. Where the amounts standing after each step tell all relata apart, the classes are fixed too (`World.classes_fixed`). `Lineage.world_readings` and `Hibernation.world_readings` keep the counterexamples: balance can admit different arisings and classes at once. The reading of holding, and reading conservation as continuation, are AI readings; no numbered decision records them. Not proved: undermining and classes under splits or merges, and sufficient conditions for a mixed census. Record: [identity-across-steps](·). Study: [section 108](·).
+### 2.1 Renewal and consumption belong to runs
+
+**In words.** A formation renews where every condition it depends on or draws on keeps supporting every formation that depends on it, and consumes where it draws on a condition from which some dependent loses support for good. The two exclude each other without exhausting the cases, and the class belongs to the run, not to a configuration or to the formation's own course: persistence, success and growth do not certify renewal.
+
+- `falls_not_recurring`: an amount counted in whole units that never rises from some step on cannot keep falling. It is the whole-number instance of the least-loss law (`Amounts.rests`, §1.3); over dense amounts a halving stock falls for ever (`Halving.approaches_without_reaching`). Depletion with no run, recurrent renewal by a rank, and drawing without renewal are its cases. Used in §4.3 (constraint 1).
+- `Renewable.class_belongs_to_the_run`: in one process, from one start, the focal formation is active at every step; in one run it renews, in another it consumes the sustaining formation's condition and that formation ends. The earlier module outside the spine has the same point (`own_trajectory_does_not_decide`). Used in §4.3.
+- *No finite history decides the class, in `Renewable`*: for every horizon two runs agree before it, and after it one renews and the other consumes, so a reading decided by finite prefixes that counts every renewing run counts a consuming one (`whole_run_includes_overdraw`); a reading by amount, taking no more than is renewed, is decided by finite histories and withholds every overdraw (`amount_reading`). This is shown for this process, not for every process; what finite stretches decide in every process is §3.2.
+- `jointly_consuming`: two formations each within renewal together consume a shared condition and both end; the class belongs to their joint relation. Used in §4.1.
+
+The stepwise reading [AI reading, D10] reads an event as within renewal where its step keeps every dependence it takes part in (`RenewingAt`), and reads `living` stepwise as "active and not undermining", undermining being drawing that leaves a condition below a need once met in the dependence's unbroken tenure (`MetAbove`). It differs from the whole-run reading both ways (an escalation, a brief dip), withholds drawing after a loss, and has a cost: `draws` carries no amount, so drawing exactly the renewed amount is withheld too; its witnesses are in [becoming-stepwise-reading](·). Return grades renewal: kept, returning within a period, returning without bound, never returning; consumption is exactly some dependence never returning (`consumed_iff`, unfolding the definition). In a family of laws where renewal depends on the renewed condition, a loss beyond the threshold does not come back (`no_return_below_support`); a supported route of contribution can repair the relation (periphery); a consumer that substitutes continues by transforming its dependence and is still consuming, the sustaining formation ending (`stepwise_includes_substitution`); in one class of wear laws the two classes are dynamically distinguishable (periphery).
+
+Records: [becoming-renewal-reading](·), [relational-renewal-classification](·), [becoming-stepwise-reading](·), [becoming-return-grades](·), [becoming-finite-horizon](·), [supported-renewal-recovery](·), [substitution-preserves-consumption](·), [renewing-consuming-formation](·), [becoming-dependence-dynamics](·).
