+### 2.3 Joint excess, taking all, and what is fed from beyond
+
+**In words.** What a family takes without end it is fed from beyond; draws each within what a step gives can together exceed it, and a joint excess that brings a level below the renewers' need ends them and everything depending on the condition at that need. A whole of parts that each end, whose parts arise only where they depend on such a condition, ends with it, whoever draws. Taking all that is given excludes every other taker, and a take that rises at every step exhausts what it takes from and ends.
+
+- `Flow.fed_from_beyond`: under balance and dissipation a finite family, listed once, from which taking recurs and which is enclosed around from some step on, cannot from any step on be fed from nothing beyond it. It needs natural-number amounts; with real amounts losses can shrink geometrically and it fails. What is needed is being fed, not the recurrence of a source (`Lone.fed_not_recurring`). Used in §4.3 (a collective fed from beyond depends on what lies beyond).
+- `Flow.excess_bounded`, `Flow.joint_excess_ends`: each step of joint excess lowers the level by at least one unit, so it cannot outlast what was held; where renewal is given only by formations depending on what they renew, a joint excess bringing the level below their need ends them and every formation depending at such a need (`Exceeding.all_end`; with one taker all continue, `Alone.all_continue`). Own draws within what is given can jointly exceed it (`Pair.own_not_joint`, `Exceeding.own_not_joint`). Used in §4.3 (relative position does not protect).
+- `Web.Whole.family_excess_ends`: a whole that draws its parts' arising beyond its renewal ends. Read on one world with a flow, a whole (`Web.Whole`, active exactly while some part is, §2.2) of parts listed at each step and each ending, whose parts arise only where they then depend on some condition of a family at a need of at least `m`, the family's renewal gated on it, has no part arising after `n` steps of excess of the family's uptake over its replenishment from a stock below `n + m`, and ends; the family of one condition is `Web.Whole.joint_excess_ends`. Below it, listed parts each ending, none arising from some step on, end together with their whole (`Web.Listed.end_without_arising`, `Web.Whole.ends_without_arising`), of which `Whole.needs_arising` is the corollary. The uptake is the joint draw: the whole need not be a taker, and its own draw within what is renewed proves nothing. The parts need not depend on the family once arisen; the whole ends once those arisen have ended. Every premise holds with a whole active for three steps (`WholeExceeding.drawn`), and the excess, ending parts and the arising's dependence are each needed (`WholeWithin.kept`, `WholeUnending.persists`, `WholeUngated.persists`). Read with a collective as the whole of its lives and their renewal as the family, this is OPENING's "one that consumes them consumes what it goes on through" under named premises [AI reading; [study §287](·)].
+- `RegimeMargin.ends_iff_below`: the margin of a regime. The margin law (§6.1) compares levels with the rest's exchanges held as they were, and on measured data that comparison holds as an identity ([MQ1, study §253](·)); what a measurement tests is the margin with the condition's own giving responding to its level. With giving read off what a standing draw `H` leaves (`RegimeMargin.step`), a level below `H + y`, where giving falls short of the draw below `y`, is gone within as many steps as it stood (`RegimeMargin.ends_below`), and from `H + y` up to a top the step keeps, the level holds (`RegimeMargin.holds`): the point of no return is exact. Where giving stops below a need, that point lies at least the draw above the need, and more exactly where giving at the need falls short of the draw (`RegimeMargin.beyond_draw_iff`), and it rises with the draw where giving does not rise (`RegimeMargin.rises_by_draw`): the need is the regime's, as MQ1 measured in the simulated yeast (1.4–4.1 times the draw above the need). On real yeast the giving law is itself the regime's: at equal density giving falls as the dilution rises ([MQ2, study §266](·), post hoc), and giving lowered by the regime raises the need beyond what removal alone gives, strictly exactly where the lowered giving falls short of the draw at the old need (`RegimeMargin.lowered_raises_strictly`). Draws add, harms do not: where giving under the joint draw is subadditive above the need and no greater than under either draw, the rise of the point of no return under two draws together is at least the sum of the rises under each, less one whole unit (`RegimeMargin.harms_superadditive`), and two draws the condition holds under alone can together end it from every level (`RegimeMargin.Peaked.together_ends`). The time to break lies between `RegimeMargin.not_before` and `RegimeMargin.falls_within`, MQ1's band. Harvesting theory states the same structure over the reals (depensation and the fold of the harvested equilibrium: Clark 1976; May 1977); the module states it in whole numbers ([margin of a regime](·)). Where giving adjusts, reading what is left and the recent giving (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.step`), the regime's step is the case reading what is left alone (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.orbit_regime`). Every rest of the state at or above the draw is the regime's wherever the adjustment rests at the draw exactly where the regime gives the draw, on the run as on the step (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.rests_iff`), so for every giving between the recent and the regime's that moves wherever it differs from the regime's (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.Between.rests_iff`). The point decides the fate where the recent giving lies on the level's side of the draw (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.ends_iff_below`); with it on the other side, what was given before carries a condition across the point both ways (`RegimeMargin.Crossing.crosses`; RM2, [study §299](·), [the regime's point under giving that adjusts](·)). Runs come to rest where the adjustment rises with what is left and with the recent giving and a band keeps the state: every run within a band up to `hi` is still within `3 hi + 3` steps, at the draw with a level the regime's step leaves as it is, or below the draw with level and recent giving equal, which is nothing where nothing gives from nothing (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.comes_to_rest`). Whether a run changes again is decided at each step, since a law's run with a bounded mark comes to rest within the bound (`LastChange.still_within`), so settling needs no omniscience here. Giving that falls as what is left rises can keep a run moving within its band for ever (`RegimeMargin.Alternation.alternates`), as overcompensating renewal cycles (May 1976) (RM3, [study §300](·), [where a run of a regime comes to rest](·)). Where the adjustment rises with what is left and with the recent giving, the point of no return is a curve in the plane of level and recent giving. A run has at most one rest (`LastChange.still_same`), and a state at or below one whose run rests below the draw rests below it too, so within a band up to `hi`, for each recent giving, the runs resting below the draw are exactly those from levels below a least level, found by a finite search with no omniscience (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.falls_iff_below`); it does not rise as the recent giving rises (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.threshold_falls`), and under the regime's step it is the point `H + y` at every recent giving (`RegimeMargin.threshold_regime`). Without giving rising with what is left, a run from a level can come to rest below the draw while one from a lower level holds, and no such level exists (`RegimeMargin.Notch.no_threshold`) (RM4, [study §301](·), [the threshold in the plane of level and recent giving](·)). None of this needs amounts to be counted. In any linearly ordered amounts with a draw taken first the step of a rising adjustment keeps the order of states, and from the first step on a step that neither raises nor lowers both climbs or sinks toward the draw, whatever the adjustment, the next such step of the same kind, while a step raising or lowering both is followed by such steps for ever (`RegimeMargin.Drawn.run_shape`); the rests are the regime's point or below the draw with level and recent giving equal (`RegimeMargin.Drawn.still_iff`). Over the non-negative reals (the periphery module `RegimeReals`, with Mathlib) every run within a band converges, to a rest where the adjustment is continuous, and the states converging below the draw are down-closed and fewer as the recent giving rises (`Drawn.converges`, `Drawn.limit_fates`, `Drawn.falls_given`). What whole numbers add is that the rest is reached in finitely many steps and the fate decided at a fixed step: giving moving halfway toward a draw of one converges and never rests (`Drawn.Relaxation.never_rests`) (RM5, [study §302](·), [the regime in any amounts](·)). A condition's point of no return is not its own where its giving reads what is left of another. Under draws taken first, two conditions each giving from what is left of both, with each giving rising with what is left of each, keep the order of states, so a condition ending from a state ends from every state below it (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.ends_of_below`). Within a band in whole numbers a run comes to rest within `2 hi + 1` steps, and for each level of its partner the first condition ends exactly below a least level, found by a finite search, which does not rise as the partner's level rises (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.ends_iff_below`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.threshold_falls`). A condition giving nothing where nothing is left of its partner falls by its draw once the partner stays within its draw, and ends within as many steps as its level (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.ends_after`); under dependence both ways the two end together. Support can carry a condition across its own point (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.MutualActivation.saves`); under inhibition more of the other can end a condition that holds alone, and the order of fates breaks (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.MutualInhibition.breaks_order`); beyond a band mutual support can hold a pair neither of which holds alone in a cycle that never rests (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Relay.cycles`). A condition whose giving reads only what is left of itself runs as the regime (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.first_regime`) (RM6, [study §306](·), [coupled regimes](·)). Coupling is not bounded to pairs. A web of any number of conditions, each giving from what is left of all, keeps the order of states under mutual support, so raising any condition's level never ends one that held (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_of_below`). Where a condition gives nothing wherever nothing is left of another, the other's end ends it, and along every chain of such dependence, every dependent's draw positive, the end of one ends everything downstream of it, however far, while a ring of mutual dependence ends together or not at all (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_downstream`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_together`). The cascade reaches a condition that does not depend directly on the first, and a draw of nothing on the chain stops it (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Chain.cascades`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Chain.stopped`). The pair is the web indexed by `Bool`, and its laws of order and dependence are read off the web's (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.pair_run`) (RM7, [study §311](·), [coupled webs](·)). For finitely many conditions within a band, stated condition by condition, which needs no equality of functions since monotone giving respects what is left condition by condition, every run comes to rest within the conditions' count times the band with one step, whether a condition ends is decided there, and each condition's point of no return, given the other levels, is a least level, exact, that does not rise as any other level rises (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.comes_to_rest`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_iff_below`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.threshold_falls`); the pair's rest and thresholds are these laws read for two (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.threshold_pair`) (RM8, [study §325](·), [rest-on-coupled-webs](·)). Beyond a band, a bound on the run takes its place: a run that stays within `B` comes back within `(B + 1)` to the conditions' count steps and repeats, so whether a condition ends is decided by a finite check, with no band and no order of states, and under mutual support each condition's point of no return is exact and does not rise as any other level rises wherever the run from its top level stays within `B` (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_iff_within`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_iff_below_within`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.threshold_falls_within`); `Relay`, which keeps no band, has its first condition's threshold fall from three to two as its partner rises from two to three (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Relay.threshold_beyond_band`) (RM9, [study §327](·), [thresholds-beyond-a-band](·)). These laws hold for any law of states read condition by condition, a law keeping the order of states so reading them, and so for a web with a recent giving, each condition holding its level and what it gave last, its giving a law of what is left of all and what each gave: under mutual support it keeps the order, so its bounded runs have ending decided and each threshold, given the other levels and every recent giving, exact and not rising as any of them rises; the plain web and the adjusted regime are its cases, and a giving ramping with what was given has its threshold fall from four to three as its last giving rises (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Recent.keepsBelow`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Recent.plain`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Recent.adjusted`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Recent.Momentum.threshold_falls_with_recent`) (RM10, [study §331](·), [webs-with-a-recent-giving](·)). Every threshold here is exact by one law: where a fate is down-closed in the level and read off an exact check, the least level from which the check fails is its point of no return, and where one fate implies another its point is no lower (`RegimeMargin.leading_exact`, `RegimeMargin.leading_falls`; UM, [study §335](·)).
+- `Flow.continuing_excludes`: a full taker (`Flow.TakesAll`) that continues leaves no other formation taking from the condition at each of `level + 1` steps; full taking alongside another taker ends every formation depending at the matching need, the full taker included (`Flow.full_taking_ends`), and a taker active only while it takes ends, the ending derived (`Flow.continuing_ends_taker`). Of `Exceeding`'s three courses, each taking one keeps all three supported: the first's continuation does not need the second's ending, taking all does (`Excluding.three_courses`), and the courses are alike by admission (`Excluding.admission_alike`), so the loss is the member's continuation [AI reading, D44].
+- `Flow.outrun_below`: where a part (the rest) takes jointly more than is given at each of `n` steps from a level below `n + m`, the level stays below `m` from then on and every formation depending at that need ends, whatever a member outside the part takes (`Flow.outrun_excess`, `Flow.outrun_ends`; full taking alongside another taker is the case of a part of two). With need one, every reading of the condition after the rest's end is alike under the member's acts (`Flow.outrun_reading_alike`), so no weight of such a reading selects its restraint. Tested on learners in a gated commons (CG2, `experiments/commons-outrun`, predictions frozen before any run): where the other members alone empty the patch, coupled learners empty it for every weight of an end reading; where they cannot, learners keep it, though the whole group at full draw would empty it.
+- `Flow.seeking_ends`: a take more than now (`MoreThanNow`, §3.4) rises by at least `n` in `n` steps (`more_accumulates`), so from a condition given at most `B` a step it takes all that is given after `B + 1` steps, and under balance a formation that takes so while active is not active through a bounded window; where its activity does not resume, it ends, derived from balance and the bound on what is given alone. Where renewal depends on what it renews, the seeker exhausts the condition for every formation depending at the matching need, renewers included (`Flow.seeking_exhausts`). In `Alone` a taker taking all without its take rising continues (`Alone.takes_all`): what ends the seeker is the rising take. Used in §3.4.
+
+What the derived extent does not reach. It runs one way, to what one's own continuation depends on: where one stops giving, a formation living on that giving ends while one continues (`Downstream.one_way`); it ends with the want (`Mortal.after_its_end`); and a clearer meeting every requirement derived here, active throughout, renewed, fed from beyond and drawing jointly within what is given, still exhausts the dweller's habitat (`Clearing.undermines_within_renewal`). The witnesses' endings are stipulated in their activity and shown consistent with balance, support and dependence; the general theorems derive endings.
+
