+### 2.4 Evolution and transmission
+
+**In words.** Evolution names specific mechanisms (transmission, reconstruction, variation, selection), each explained through its own relations; it is not a synonym for every change. On the spine, descent is defined by taking part, giving and coming to stand as a condition, with no valuation.
+
+- `price`: Price's equation in counting form, an arithmetic identity for any finite family of parents and offspring; the weighted total is not the selection term proper (`selected_uniform`).
+- `SelectionTerm.covariation`: the selection term proper, with no premise: over any finite family, the number of parents times the offspring-weighted amounts, with the pairs where more offspring go with less amount, is the number of offspring times the parents' total, with the pairs where more go with more, the covariance with its denominators cleared; with `price` it is Price's equation with its selection term (`SelectionTerm.offspring_covariation`). Over generations each the offspring of the last, the mean amount is kept or rises across a step exactly where selection proper and transmission balance or raise (`Generations.kept_step_iff`, `Generations.rises_step_iff`), and a moved mean has an unbalanced step, found by deciding each (`Generations.moved_unbalanced`): with exact transmission one with selection proper, with uniform offspring numbers one with inexact transmission. Where only active formations give and activity needs support, a reading highest at the supported parents is never selected against (`SelectionTerm.Flow.support_not_against`); over generations of descent its mean, never lowered by transmission, does not fall, and with exact transmission moves only upward through a step of selection proper (`SelectionTerm.Flow.support_not_lower`, `SelectionTerm.Flow.support_moved_rises`); `Drawdown`'s flow meets these premises (`SupportedDescent.supported_descent`).
+- `Reproduction.variation`: selection on offspring number itself, with no premise: read on the weights themselves no pair is discordant, so the number of members times the total of the squared weights is the square of the total weight with the squared differences over pairs, equal exactly where the weights are uniform (`Reproduction.none_iff_uniform`); with offspring numbers, over offspring the mean of their parent's offspring number is at least the mean over parents (`Reproduction.number_variation`). Over generations read by offspring number, the mean offspring number does not fall where transmission lowers none, and with exact transmission rises exactly where offspring numbers vary (`Generations.ByNumber.not_lower_step`, `Generations.ByNumber.rises_exact_iff`): the counting form of Fisher's fundamental theorem with exact transmission. A parent's offspring number is at most what it gives them (`Reproduction.Flow.born_le_given`) and, its offspring distinct within a family dissipated on, with one more at most what it takes from the family (`Reproduction.Flow.number_within_take`); distinct offspring standing within a family balanced and dissipated on number, with its takers, at most its stock (`Reproduction.Flow.born_within_stock`). A lineage within such a family reproduces at most its stock many steps and ends (`Reproduction.Flow.lineage_ends`), so read by offspring number one that began reproducing has a step at which transmission lowered offspring number by more than selection on it and what it raised (`Reproduction.Flow.closed_lineage_lowered`); without dissipation a lossless relay keeps a lineage going (`Reproduction.Relay.relay`). The additive part: counted, Cauchy–Schwarz holds over any finite list (`Reproduction.bound_sq`), so the concordance with the discordance of offspring number with any carried amount, squared, is at most the squared differences of offspring numbers over pairs times those of the amount (`Reproduction.additive_le`, `Reproduction.covariance_sq_le`): the additive part of the variance in offspring number through the amount is at most the whole, all of it where the amount is offspring number itself (`Reproduction.additive_self`), and with exact transmission the rise of the amount's mean is bounded so (`Reproduction.Generations.response_sq_le`); an amount can vary beside varying offspring numbers with no covariance (`Reproduction.Unrelated.unrelated`). Mutation, transmission that is not exact: carriers leaving k offspring that carry an amount and m that do not, the others w, the carriers' share rises exactly where d·k exceeds c·m + d·w (`Reproduction.Mutation.rises_iff`), never where k ≤ w and with any loss falls at every step (`Reproduction.Mutation.never_rises`, `Reproduction.Mutation.falls_of_outrun`: the error threshold), is kept at s/(s+m) where k = w + s (`Reproduction.Mutation.kept_share`) and approached from below without overshoot (`Reproduction.Mutation.below_always`); read as generations of descent, transmission lowers the amount by c·m and the step is balanced exactly there (`Reproduction.Mutation.balanced_iff`): mutation–selection balance is Price's balance of selection against transmission. Several carried amounts at once: an amount combining them that reproduces, `d` times, offspring number's covariation with each (the normal equations with denominators cleared) has `d` times its covariation with offspring number equal to its own spread (`Reproduction.Breeding.breeding_balance`), at most `d²` times offspring number's (`Reproduction.Breeding.additive_part_le`), and with exact transmission `d` times the cross-multiplied rise of its mean is that spread (`Reproduction.Breeding.response`): Fisher's fundamental theorem with breeding values, one carried amount its case (`Reproduction.Breeding.one_amount`); an offspring number that is the product of two amounts leaves a part no combination carries (`Reproduction.Interaction.interaction`).
+- `SelectionLevels.levels`: selection within groups and among them, with no premise beyond groups of equal size: over a family listed as k groups, the whole's concordance, with k times the groups' own discordance and the discordance among groups read by their totals, is the whole's discordance with k times the groups' own concordance and the concordance among groups; divided through, the whole's covariance is the mean of the groups' covariances with the covariance of their means, the multilevel form of Price's equation. So an amount selected against within the groups is selected for in the whole only where selection among them goes for it (`SelectionLevels.among_for_of_rises`), and over listed generations with exact transmission its mean rises only there (`SelectionLevels.among_for_of_raises`); with the same within-group counts the whole goes either way (`SelectionLevels.AmongWins.among_wins`, `SelectionLevels.WithinWins.within_wins`).
+- `SelectionLevels.levels_sized`: selection within groups and among them for groups of any sizes. With n a common multiple of the sizes and each group's own term by n over its size, n squared times the whole's term balances n times the whole's size times the groups' own terms with the term of the groups' means read member by member; divided through, the whole's covariance is the size-weighted mean of the groups' covariances with the size-weighted covariance of their means, and `SelectionLevels.levels` is its case with equal sizes. Read by their totals, groups of unequal size can show nothing among them while their means carry all the whole's selection (`SelectionLevels.ByMeans.by_means`). Where the groups' means are alike nothing is selected among them, so a generation listed as groups alike in mean raises its mean exactly as selection within them goes (`SelectionLevels.rises_exact_iff_within_of_alike`): how the next generation is listed does not enter a step, but it fixes the next step's among-group part. Ending fixes that part for any sizes (`GroupEnding.Flow.rises_iff_inactive_sized`), and can use it up: with two keeping groups beside a group leaving nothing, holding back rises by selection among groups, the offspring of each keeping group form groups alike in it, and at the next step it falls below where it started (`GroupEnding.Exhausted.next_step`). Groups formed by descent keep it: with exact transmission the lineages of groups uniform in an amount keep the value each was founded at (`SelectionLevels.lineage_value`) and list every later generation (`SelectionLevels.lineages_whole`), so nothing is selected within them and the mean rises exactly where the lineages' means select for the amount (`SelectionLevels.rises_iff_lineages`), the complete-assortment end of reading group selection by assortment (Hamilton 1975). On the base, where at each step the lineages founded lower are not active, the mean never falls below where it started, over any number of steps (`GroupEnding.Flow.lineages_not_lower`), and rises wherever a higher lineage leaves offspring beside a lower one (`GroupEnding.Flow.lineages_raises`); with the groups of `Exhausted` formed by descent instead, holding back rises and stays (`GroupEnding.Assorted.kept`). Whether selection among groups accumulates or falls back is fixed by how the next groups are formed. Between the two ends, groups founded mixed: where each unit a member keeps gives `b` to every member of its group and takes `c` from the keeper, selection within goes against keeping by `b + c` times the groups' own spreads (`SelectionLevels.within_returns`), selection among them goes for it exactly where `b + c` falls short of `m` times `b` (`SelectionLevels.among_for_iff`), and the whole selects for it exactly where `b + c` times the whole's spread falls short of `m b` times the spread among groups (`SelectionLevels.rises_iff_returns`, from `SelectionLevels.returns_balance`): with the assortment the share of the spread among groups, Hamilton's rule (Hamilton 1964, 1975), stated in counts with nothing subtracted. The same returns give either verdict by how the groups are founded (`SelectionLevels.Founding.either_verdict`), and assortment below one can lose where assortment one would win (`SelectionLevels.Partly.below_one`).
+- `GroupEnding.rises_iff_ended`: selection among groups by ending: where every group with less of an amount than another leaves no offspring, nothing is discordant among the groups, so the whole selects for the amount exactly where k times the within-group discordance is below k times the within-group concordance with the concordance among groups; with groups uniform in it, never against it (`GroupEnding.not_against_of_ended`). On the base, where only active formations give, a member depending on a condition whose gated renewal ran into joint excess leaves no descendant from then on (`GroupEnding.Flow.excess_childless`, through `Flow.joint_excess_ends`), and over generations of descent with exact transmission the mean rises where the groups with less of the amount are such groups (`GroupEnding.Flow.raises_of_inactive`), and with groups not uniform it rises exactly where k times the within-group discordance is below k times the within-group concordance with the concordance among groups (`GroupEnding.Flow.rises_iff_inactive`); one condition shared by every group, once it ends them, leaves the next generation empty, so it supplies no selection among them (`GroupEnding.Flow.all_end`).
+- `Flow.family_excess_ends`, `GroupEnding.Flow.coupled_end_together`: groups whose conditions are coupled. The joint count and the gated ending hold of a family of conditions read as one: a step at which the family's uptake exceeds its replenishment lowers its stock by at least one (`Flow.family_excess_bounded`), and where whatever gives to a member depends on some member at a need of at least m (the coupled gate), n such steps from a stock below n + m end every formation depending on any member at such a need; the laws of one condition (`Flow.joint_excess_ends` and those it rests on) are this law for the family of that condition alone. A patch renewed by a neighbour shows no joint excess read alone and its renewal is not gated on it, while read as one with the neighbour it is gated, in excess, and both formations end (`Coupled.alone_within`, `Coupled.alone_ungated`, `Coupled.all_end`): the commons test's scope prediction on the spine. Groups whose members depend on conditions of one such family end together, each leaving no offspring and nothing selected among them; where the groups with less of an amount depend on such a family they leave nothing (`GroupEnding.Flow.ended_of_family`). So ending selects among groups only between families.
+- `Founding.Flow.confined_ends`: selection within a whole and a lineage confined to it. Where a family of conditions ran into excess under the coupled gate, every member of a later generation of descent is the offspring of a member that depended on no condition of the family at the gate's need (`Founding.Flow.survivors_independent`), and a lineage every later member of which depends on the family has no member after its end, however far selection within had raised it. A rise (`Founding.Flow.Rise`: an amount marking the lineage that selection within goes for, the lineage taking from the family during its excess) whose lineage is confined to the family (`Founding.Flow.ConfinedRise`) ends so (`Founding.Flow.ConfinedRise.ends`; the rise's other clauses do not enter). In `Founding.Body` two lineages each meet every clause of a rise on one body (`Founding.Body.confined_rise`, `Founding.Body.spread_rise`); the confined one ends (`Founding.Body.confined_ended`), and the one whose descendant depends on a condition outside the body still has a member a generation after every part depending on the body has ended (`Founding.Body.spread_unconfined`, `Founding.Body.spread_outlasts`). In generations founded uniform, selection within at a step needs transmission that raised or lowered the amount at some step before it (`Founding.varied_before`). Read over wholes each founded by one part (`Founding.Nested.Founded`), what transmission raised and lowered across a generation of wholes is how far the next founders moved from their founder within the whole (`Founding.Nested.raises_iff_carried`, the transmission term of Price 1970); where every next founder carries its founder's value (`Founding.Nested.Sequestered`), the mean founding value rises exactly where selection among wholes goes for it, whatever happened within (`Founding.Nested.raises_iff_among`, the exact case of `Generations.raises_exact_iff`), and without that the change within can outweigh selection among wholes (`Founding.Germline.unsequestered_falls`). Read (the AI's reading) as cancer and as a germ line, these are known results (Buss 1987; Michod 1999; Michod and Roze 2001; Aktipis et al. 2015) restated with the flow; removal of parts by the whole's rule, and how parts first come to live as one, are not stated.
+- `Drift.falls_back`: drift, offspring sampled rather than listed. A next generation of two kinds drawn n times from p listed offspring of the first kind and q of the second, each sampling a course of `Typicality` weighed by the ways of drawing it: on average the sampled share is the listed share (`Drift.expected_ones`), and the squared deviations add to n·p·q·(p+q)^n (`Typicality.spread`). Where a listed step raises the share from h/N to p/(p+q) by the gap g = N·p − (p+q)·h, the samplings falling back to h/N or below weigh, times n²·g², at most N²·n·p·q·(p+q)^n: out of the whole, at most p·q/((p+q)²·δ²·n) with δ = p/(p+q) − h/N. They weigh at least q^n, the samplings losing the first kind (`Drift.lost_weight`, `Drift.falls_back_ge`), so undoing selection is rare as the sample grows and at no size ruled out. Over listed generations the same holds for a step raising the mean of an amount held or not (`Drift.Generations.raised_falls_back`), and on the base where that step is ending among groups (`Drift.Flow.ended_falls_back`). Counting weighs the samplings and does not say which happens. Over many generations, each sampled from the last (`Drift.sampled`), the final count summed over the histories is its start times the whole weight (`Drift.sampled_count`), the ends absorb (`Drift.sampled_none`, `Drift.sampled_all`), the histories still varied after k generations weigh at most r^k with r + 2 = N^N (`Drift.varied_vanishes`), and the histories fixing the first kind have, times N, a share within N·r^k/(N^N)^k below h (`Drift.fixation`): drift alone ends variation and fixes each kind with its starting share h/N. With selection in the draw, replacement one at a time among M + 1 (up with weight a, down with b, only the steps that change the count read; `Drift.Replacement.value`), the potential with steps b^j·a^(M−j) keeps its weighted value over any number of steps (`Drift.Replacement.value_potential`), so the fixation share tends to its value at the start over its value at the top (`Drift.Replacement.fixation`), the Moran fixation probability in counts: the starting share where a = b (`Drift.Replacement.neutral_share`), at least it where b ≤ a and strictly above it from every mixed start where b < a (`Drift.Replacement.favoured_share`, `Drift.Replacement.favoured_share_above`), and the favoured kind lost with weight at least b^i (`Drift.Replacement.lost_ge`).
+- `unsupported_childless`: where only active formations give and activity needs support, an unsupported formation leaves no descendants, and the parents' weighted need is bounded by the level (`selected_le`).
+- `transmitted_supported`: where descendants take up their parents' dependences (`TransmitsWithin`, a premise), a transmitted need exceeds the level at the giving step by at most the bound of transmission (`Slack`); in `Drawdown` transmission, variation, selection and the feedback of activity on selection lie in one unfolding. Used in §3.4 (`share_rises`) and §4.5 (passing).
+
+Transmission is inheritance and need, and is independent where it binds (`Becoming.Transmission`). Fitness is not defined: offspring number is read as a weight and, bounded by what is given and taken, as an amount the flow fixes (`Becoming.Reproduction`); mutation, drift and population dynamics are not covered. The periphery mechanisms (inherited structural copying, formed copying and its correction, growth-constrained fragmentation, inherited organizational rules; standard Lean axioms) keep their own scope, and no correspondence between them and this content is proved; the growth case is restated on the base in `Becoming.Cuts` (§2.5). Prepared material joins recurrent chain formation (periphery): a copy of a word produces the word exactly when the pool supplies it and the support covers what it draws, and where every unit draws d from one stock and becomes two, n rounds from k units run exactly when the stock covers d·k(2^n − 1) (`Copying.built_iff`, `RecurrentAssembly.supported_rounds`). See [the theory of evolution](·) and [evolutionary organization](·).
