-- *The gap for one's own act* ([Becoming.SelectionGap](·), [the-gap-for-ones-own-act](·)). Where the rest follows one law of exchange reading through coupling, an act whose difference stays beyond the actor's coupling closure is selected alike, with and without it, by every selection through any member of the closure, the actor among them, at every step (`Flow.act_unselected`, `Flow.act_unselected_of_coupled`). So a consequence of the act, holding with it and failing without it, is a selection through no member of the closure (`Flow.consequence_unselected`). The rest's response is derived from the law (`ExchangeLaw.Through.responds`), not supplied; where both acts are laws, the courses the law generates with each are compared and nothing is supplied (`act_courses_unselected`). `Clearing` is a world in which such an act ends a formation within the actor's reach. Study: [section 176](·).
-- In `Diversion`, a flow that reaches beyond the registration closure, taking from the source a dweller depends on to raise a store the taker registers, is selected over the restrained flow by a selection through the taker's registration. Every selection through that registration treats it alike with a raise that does not reach beyond (`Diversion.favours`, `Diversion.blind_to_source`).
-- *Raising what couples in draws from beyond* ([Becoming.SelectionReach](·), [raising-what-couples-in-draws-from-beyond](·)). The favour in `Diversion` is a law of any balanced flow. Where a family containing what couples in gains nothing across a step (nothing from nothing, `Flow.GainlessOn`), a rise of what couples in has a formation that gives it more than it takes from it and takes from beyond it (`Flow.Balances.rise_draws_beyond`); with equality decided, from a named condition outside it (`Flow.Balances.rise_takes_beyond`); and it is paid from beyond in full, the rise at most what is taken beyond it (`Flow.Balances.rise_paid_from_beyond`). So, where the family lists what a group couples into, every selection holding only where it rises holds only on flows in which a formation takes from a condition no member of the group couples into (`Flow.favours_reaching_beyond`). `Diversion` is an instance (`Diversion.draws_beyond`), and its supplying flow, which gains, raises the store with nothing taken: the premise binds (`Diversion.supplying_raises_untaken`). Study: [section 177](·).
-- *What pooled coupling reaches* ([Becoming.SelectionPool](·), [what-pooled-coupling-reaches](·)). A pool's coupling closure is the union of its members' (`withinClosureOf_iff`). With the rest of the exchange fixed and balance on what the closure couples into, every selection through the pooled coupling of any group within it selects the levels with and without a part beyond it alike (`Flow.unselected_beyond_pool`); the pooled form above is the case of a pool within one formation's closure (`Flow.unselected_beyond_coupling_all_of_pool`). Some pooled selection separates two histories exactly when the members do not all couple them alike (`Web.separates_all_iff`), and, with the members listed and each member's coupling decided, exactly when some member couples them apart (`Web.separates_all_iff_member`). An act whose difference stays beyond a pool's coupling closure, the pool's own joint act included, is selected alike by every selection through the pooled coupling of any group within the closure (`Flow.act_unselected_pool`, `act_courses_unselected_pool`); a formation whose admission the act changes lies beyond the closure and separates the act through every pool holding it (`Flow.act_selected_by_pool`). In `Clearing`, with the rest's law derived, pooling with the dweller closes the clearer's gap (`Clearing.pool_closes_gap`). Stated in §7.3 and §7.4. Study: [section 179](·).
-- *What a pool's acts respond to* ([Becoming.PoolResponse](·), [what-a-pools-acts-respond-to](·)). Where a law of exchange reads through the coupling of each formation outside a part, what a group outside the part decides by its acts is a selection through its pooled coupling (`ExchangeLaw.Through.selectsThroughAll`), so the laws above hold of what a pool does. The bound is exact where the coupling classes are decided (`ExchangeLaw.acts_alike_all_iff`), and coupling does not fix the response: the law that exchanges nothing reads through every coupling (`ExchangeLaw.response_not_fixed_by_coupling`). Under the conditions of the gap for a pool's act, nothing within the pool's coupling closure outside the acting part responds to the act (`Flow.response_alike_pool`; with both acts laws, `act_courses_response_alike_pool`). A pool meets a part's responsive reach exactly where the part meets the pool's closure (`Flow.pool_within_response_iff`), and no member responds before a difference has entered what it couples into (`TimedResponse.pool_alike_before`). In `Clearing` what every pool holding the dweller separates goes unresponded outside the clearer's part (`Clearing.separated_unresponded`); in `Loop` a response returns through the actor's coupling closure (`Loop.response_returns`). Stated in §7.4 and §7.7. Study: [section 184](·).
-- Where a selection gives the parents it holds for more offspring, their share rises among the offspring, an application of `share_rises` (`share_rises_through`).
