-**Selection revises registration.** Reconstruction within one process can change what later activity distinguishes. Where the old registration is an equivalence, every selection expressible through the old registration remains expressible through the new one exactly when new indistinguishability implies old indistinguishability. The condition composes along actual histories and directly reuses the selection through registration of `Web`. One instance, controlled by current support and the state of an apparatus, actually forms a distinguishing relation, replenishes the support used up and changes the response; the process also allows the relation to be closed. Discrimination, retained record and executable revision do not substitute for one another. The construction recipe, the reconstruction preference, the target and the replenishment remain supplied; that they are acquired by the process, or attract generally, is not derived. Record: [selection-under-registration-revision](·). Study: [the common-organization study](·).
-
-**Consequences revise the next reference plan.** The interface left open by the fixed instance above now has a conditional construction. An actual failure receipt changes the retained contact sequence. The controller executes the new sequence and acquires references; a new record is installed only once a check passes, and then the actual response changes. A mismatch elsewhere revises the plan again, and support is not reset across the history. The newly available distinctions rejoin the same `Through` by the contact domain actually installed, and preservation of old selections directly reuses the registration revision above. Frozen old plans, erased receipts, insufficient support, references that do not separate, and drift after the check keep their failures. Contact primitives, faithful return, the Boolean or stable correspondence and the revision rule remain supplied. Completing this local interface is not arbitrary invention of senses, nor the whole meta-attractor theory. Record: [consequence-revised-reference-plan](·). Study: [handover and counter-review](·).
-
-**Formation and continuing revision joined.** The [integrated account](·) directly reuses the primitive operations of the reference-plan revision. Actual response first forms from an empty method and a reference apparatus; the productive return of successful activity then pays for succession and the next round of revision. `continuing` is an actual infinite `Run` in the same controller: every round acquires fresh references and actually uses them, and cumulative use and return are not reset. The account has 36 new theorems and 62 source declarations, with empty axiom reports. Cutting the return, freezing the method, or exhausting a tight reserve breaks the continuation; retiring an old contact really loses a distinction. The return law, faithful contact, the task and the correspondence of succession remain explicit. Continuing activity is not taken as normative warrant, nor as perpetual motion from a closed finite stock.
