-**Learning: induction, generalization, training and the meta level.** Ren asked how completely the meta level, artificial neural networks, cognition and the wisdom about learning are explained, and then wrote: “please, fully complete, 我觉得理更像是对结构和变化的规律的建模 finish wisdom root, and resolve the undissolved” (the Chinese: “I think 理 is more like the modeling of the laws of structure and change”; [source](·); [Becoming.Learning](·)). A registered sequence is a sequence of registered values, such as the registration of a determined law's orbit. A learner is any claim made from the record before step t.
-
-- *No record fixes the next value.* With no premise, no record fixes the next value, even among finite worlds (`no_prefix_fixes_next`, `no_prefix_fixes_next_finite`). For every learner, some sequence answers it at every step and refutes each of its claims; that sequence keeps its record, so it is open (`diagonal_misses`, `diagonal_unrested`, `diagonal_open`).
-- *Learning by refutation.* Hold hypotheses in order and move to the next exactly where the one held is refuted. Such learning never passes a hypothesis that holds (`index_le_of_accords`).
-- *Finite worlds.* Where a list holds a determined law's orbit, its registration repeats periodically from some step on (`lasso_of_held`). Consider a learner that knows neither the configurations nor their number and reads only a registration whose values it can tell apart. It is refuted fewer than `tri N` times for N configurations; it claims at every step from step N on; and it is not the case that it is refuted at arbitrarily late steps (`held_byElimination_bounded`). That it comes to rest cannot be refuted (`held_rest_unrefuted`, a double negation). It rests only on such sequences (`lasso_of_rest`), and its record never shows that it has come to rest (`no_prefix_fixes_next_finite`).
-- *Classes.* Learning over classes is the same learning over a merged enumeration, and every merging has its diagonal sequence (`merged_bound`, `merged_unrested`).
-- *理 as modeling.* Following Ren, 理 is read as the modeling of the laws of structure and change. A model of structure is a lumping (`Lumped`); a model of change is a lumping across which the step goes alike; the two are one notion (`goAlike_iff_lumped`).
-- *Generalization.* Among the functions that go alike across a lumping, finite data fix an untried value exactly where it is lumped with some observed input (`determines_lumped_iff`). The generalization is right exactly where the world takes one value at the two (`lumped_right_iff`). An outcome of a law of change transfers exactly where the two configurations go alike by the move (`transfer_right_iff`). The class of all functions is free at every untried input, so data alone fix nothing there (`every_determines_nothing`).
-- *Training.* Training is selection through the data (`Training.loss_through`; the selection through registration of `Becoming.Selection` is an instance). In a class free beyond the data, it leaves the untried value as free as the class (`Training.unselected_beyond_data`). A fit is right beyond the data exactly where the class is determined there by the data (`Training.fit_right_iff`).
-- *Periphery bridge.* [LearningCorrespondence](·) (periphery; standard Lean axioms) reads the acquisition chain's transfer as generalization through a lumping of laws (`uniform_determines`, `nonuniform_not_determined`). Hebbian development and the route of updating are the `adaptive` systems of `Becoming.Mechanism`: activity alone, or the network alone, has no law exactly where the weights or the route make a difference (`hebbian_no_activity_law`, `updating_no_network_law`).
-
-*Readings* [AI reading, D26]. Induction is resolved into laws, not certified. The uniformity of nature is not a premise of the theory. It is the local hypothesis `Lumped`, named where it is used: that the world goes alike across what the model lumps. For a trained network the class is what training can reach, and generalization comes from the lumping that architecture and updates impose, not from the loss. The meta level is learning again, with no top. Records: [learning-by-refutation](·), [generalization-through-lumping](·). Study: [section 92](·).
