-*Reading* [AI reading, D40]. The prefix alone fixes the future through the map; what a learnable target adds to it is a reading of that future, which a learner given nothing does not have. So what `fromLaw` is given beyond the prefix serves only as a reading of a future the prefix already fixes. The witness that no learner given nothing rests on every learnable target is elementary; the content is what the prefix does fix. This holds in worlds a list holds: over every course, no prefix fixes the next value. That reading is a finite object: at most N labelled names of N − 1 values, whose labels are values the feature takes. Records: [what-an-extrapolation-given-nothing-fixes](·), [what-finitely-many-labels-fix](·). Study: [section 173](·), [section 182](·).
