-**Weights count situations.** Ren, 16 October 2026: “we are describing what everything obeys, but at every moment, the actual change depends on the situation … just saying we are all one doesn't make it true, the situation makes it true” ([source](·)). `Becoming.Weighted` does not say where weights come from, and `Becoming.Typicality` does not derive that the course which happens is typical. This states, with no premise, what natural weights are when each step is taken in as many situations as its weight, each fixing the step. The law whose moves are the situations is determined and takes exactly the steps of positive weight (`Situations.finerLaw_determined`, `Situations.finerLaw_step_iff`, [Becoming.Situations](·)): a law whose steps are those of positive weight is this determined law with the situation forgotten. For every process with listed moves and configurations and natural weights of steps, summing any reading of the courses over the finer courses is summing it over the courses, each times its weight (`Situations.sum_finer`), so the finer courses number the sum over histories (`Situations.finer_count`). On two values with p and q situations a step, there are (p + q)ⁿ finer courses, and the weight of a course is the number of situations that take it (`Situations.situations_count`, `Situations.situations_of_course`); those whose course deviates by at least d number, times d, at most n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ (`Situations.situations_typical`). So the law of large numbers counts situations: of the situations of a kind, most give frequencies near the ratio of the weights; which situation happens is not a count, and nothing here fixes it. Weights that are not natural numbers are not numbers of situations: signed weights cancel, and numbers of situations do not (`Interference.cancels`, `counting_transfer_iff`); signed weights are pairs of numbers of situations, as the next paragraph states. Reading (the AI's reading of Ren's words, which Ren took on 16 October 2026): the cor