-**The open proofs of parting and counting.** Ren, 16 October 2026: “take 2, and do the open proofs” ([source](·)). The proofs the two paragraphs above left open are given here, with no premise beyond what each law names. Where runs part only before step T and never after, the registered values decided, no two runs part from where a run is at T (`Parting.unparted_at_of_late`); held by N configurations its course has at most T + N states, and the learner by the least bound is right from 2(T + N) − 1 on (`Parting.late_statesBelow`, `Parting.late_right`). The converse: for a process with listed moves and configurations and decided steps and registered values, the learner given the world reads from the record the configurations a run from s can be at, takes the first from which a path as long as the list of configurations is open (such a path goes on without end: where a list of N holds every configuration, a course of N steps from a configuration gives courses of every length, with no decidability and no selection, `Parting.unbounded_of_continues`, on `Lasting.Continues`; `Parting.liveRun`), and claims what it registers. It is right at a step on every run from s exactly where no two such runs part there (`Parting.world_right_iff`), so some learner is right there exactly where none part (`Parting.some_right_iff`). With `Parting.not_right_on_both`, at each step a parting is exactly what neither the record nor the world settles. Concentration is exponential: for every u ≥ v, the courses with at least k ones weigh, times uᵏ·vⁿ, at most (p·u + q·v)ⁿ·vᵏ (`Typicality.concentrated`, the counting form of Chernoff's bound); with p = q = 1, of the 2ⁿ courses those with at least k ones number, times 3ᵏ, at most 4ⁿ (`Typicality.few_far_ahead`). For k ≥ 3n/4 this is a share below 0.88ⁿ, a corollary computed by hand from the theorem, not stated in Lean; the bound by the spread falls only as 1/n. Through an event, any number of values counts as two, the event's weight and the rest's in place of p and q (`Situations.sum_event`), so the law of large numbers and exponential concentration count situations for every event (`Situations.event_typical`, `Situations.event_concentrated`); each value is an event, so in most situations each value's frequency is near its share of the weight. For every process, the finer courses taking a course number its weight times how often it is listed, its weight where every move and configuration is listed once (`Situations.situations_take`, `Situations.situations_of_course_listed`). In any weights, steps weighing the sum over their situations are counted by them (`Situations.sum_finer_weights`); a signed step (P, N) is P situations that add and N that subtract, and the signed transfer is the pair of the numbers of finer courses composing to adding and to subtracting (`Situations.signed_counts`). Where signed weights cancel, the situations do not: the balanced (1, 1) of `Interference.cancels` is two situations (`Situations.cancels_situations`). Not added: real or complex amplitudes, and which situation happens. Records: [identification-where-runs-part](·), [typicality-by-counting](·), [weights-count-situations](·). Study: [section 150](·).
