-### 6.4 Reasons addressed to every position
-
-**D follows from A.** The positioned articulation D, which is not conditioned on endorsement, follows from A and from the significance of living significance, which carries no standpoint index (`positioned_articulation_of_articulates`).
-
-**A universal reason.** A sound inquiry aimed at new living content gives every position with access to it a contributory reason (`universal_reason`). Its normative premises are the seed, relational neutrality and standpoint neutrality (together `Valuation.Grounds`) and A. Connection (under the discipline of section 6.3, relative to a run) and soundness are facts about the unfolding and the inquiry ([metaethical-core-characterization](·), reusing [positioned-positive-reason](·) and [positive-ground-open-futures](·)). The theorem passes the normative content of A and of the grounds through; it does not supply it.
-
-**A reason is not more than a reason.** A contributory reason is not a duty and not a ranking, and it predicts no recognition or compliance.
