+### 6.2 What living significance says, for any significance
+
+**In words.** On a connected whole with some standpoint and some living claim, living significance for every standpoint is exactly a seed (some living claim significant from some standpoint) with two boundary neutralities: relational (significance passes along every formed relation to a living claim) and standpoint (what has significance from one standpoint has it from every one). Where every living claim is held by some standpoint, it is exactly self-significance at every standpoint with standpoint neutrality. Every premise is needed, and each rival keeps the same rule inside a boundary already formed. The dynamics fix the extent a center must count, not the center.
+
+- `Valuation.significant_iff`: the characterization. Each neutrality is the rule holding at every instance (`Neutral`), so everything living significance adds beyond what an evaluator holds lies in the two neutralities; the direction to the premises is a projection, and the content is the converse and minimality. Any position holding self-significance (`Valuation.SelfSignificance`) with living content of its own supplies a seed (`Valuation.Seed`), which is weaker.
+- `Model.seed_is_needed` with `Model.connection_is_needed`: dropping the seed, either neutrality, connection or A each leaves a consistent countermodel (`Model.relational_neutrality_is_needed`, `Model.standpoint_neutrality_is_needed`, `Model.articulation_neutrality_is_needed`). The rival holds the rule only within its own region, its own standpoint, or those who endorse; the present-aim evaluator, with no seed, values nothing; a living claim outside every formed relation is reached by no transmission. That every rival is the same rule inside a boundary is a framing of these countermodels, not a theorem about all rivals. For rivals that weigh what can form additively it is exact: a weighting that counts every formation ranks as C does wherever C ranks and decides only mixed comparisons, and one that gives some formation weight zero is a boundary (`Weighting.widens_iff_every_positive`, `Weighting.weighed_eq_of_unweighted`; [THE-STEP-OF-INVARIANCE §6.5](·)). Non-additive orders, priority weighted by how well off each is in the outcome, and deontic constraints beyond not closing are not modelled (§8.9), and Sidgwick's dualism of practical reason is located, not dissolved, at boundary neutrality.
+- `Valuation.significant_iff_held`: where every living claim is held (`Valuation.Held`), living significance is self-significance everywhere with standpoint neutrality, with neither connection nor relational neutrality; with lives no standpoint holds, relational neutrality is added for the unheld only (`Valuation.significant_iff_reached`); each premise is needed (`Apart.not_enough`, `Unclaimed`, `Relayed`). On a connected whole where every standpoint holds a living claim, self-significance with relational neutrality also gives it (`Valuation.significant_of_transmits`): standpoint neutrality is the completion needing no connection, not the only one. Read stepwise, with each formation's region its closure under any relation, every living event is held (`Web.selfValuation_held`, `Web.selfValuation_significant_iff`; along the empty relation, `Web.significant_iff_self`).
+- `Clearing.center_not_derived`: in `Clearing`, each formation holds and values its own events and the clearer also its source's; every life is held, self-significance holds everywhere, each standpoint's significance is closed under feeding, and the dweller's living event has no significance from the clearer's standpoint. Along every formed relation of the stepwise reading the extent would reach the dweller; that the source requires nothing is stipulated. Self-significance ranges over living claims only, so a formation's own undermining events fall outside it (`Clearing.clearer_not_living`). Used in §6.4.
+- `Conditions.significant_iff_of_common`: under a correspondence discipline, a common condition every living formation takes part in connects the whole, and there living significance is a seed with both neutralities; disjoint conditions can disconnect it (`Separate.not_connected`). The discipline relates two events through a condition only where one draws on it and the other depends on it at a positive level, so an idle condition connects nothing (`Web.inert_connects`) and connection is made by living use (`Shared.connection_by_living_use`), though a renewed condition used once still connects (`one_use_connects`). Under relational neutrality valuing a consumer's activity reaches every living event of what it consumes (`Conditions.valuing_consumption_reaches`; stepwise, `Web.valuing_breaking_reaches`).
+
+*Further relations and readings of `living`.* Living on (drawing on a relatum and depending on it at a positive need) and descent (taking part in the step a relatum begins to stand and giving to it) connect a bee and a flower and generations each given by the one before; under relational neutrality valuing the fox's eating reaches the hare's living; living on needs actual drawing and a dependence that can fail, and the relatum lived on need be neither embodied nor active (`Drowsy`). Conveyance relates two events at a step (`Flow.conveyance`); an idle relatum is related to none, the boundary of a continuing family is crossed from every step on (`Flow.region_not_a_cut`), and valuing a relatum's event reaches what conveys into it (`Flow.valuing_reaches_source`). Readings are relative to a run (`Renewable.class_belongs_to_the_run`); whole-run and stepwise readings differ only in `living`, both ways (`Renewable.readings_differ`), and an event's stepwise reading is the conjunction of its relations' (`Web.living_iff_relations`). In the renewable process a finite-prefix reading counting every whole-run renewing run counts a consuming one (`Renewable.finite_reading_includes_consumption`), and a whole-run but-for test of a single part cannot replace participation (`Overdetermined.no_difference`, `Renewable.no_finite_segment_makes_difference`). Whether conditions such as the biosphere or the climate are shared by all living formations is an empirical correspondence; whether the relational reading is 生生 is a philosophical argument, and its ground is not established ([assessment](·); the comparison of readings in [study §8.5](·)).
+
+*Reasons addressed to every position.* The positioned articulation D, not conditioned on endorsement, follows from A with positive content read as significance from every standpoint (`positioned_articulation_of_articulates`). A sound inquiry aimed at new living content gives every position with access to it a contributory reason (`universal_reason`): its normative premises are the seed, both neutralities (together `Valuation.Grounds`) and A, while connection and soundness are facts about the unfolding and the inquiry; the theorem passes the normative content through and does not supply it. A contributory reason is not a duty or a ranking, and predicts no recognition or compliance. Used in §7.4.
+
+*Readings* [AI reading, D1, D9, D10, D11, D12, D13, D15, D43]. Ren's answer to what makes ethical quality: “我的答案是生生不息 - 一种整体的，不断创造更多生的方向，而这个方向产生的可能性，多样性越高，复杂性/复杂结构的复杂度可以不断的上升，就是一个好的方向” ([source](·); “My answer is 生生不息, generation of life without ceasing: a direction of the whole that keeps creating more life. The more possibilities and diversity this direction produces, and the more the complexity of complex structures can keep rising, the better a direction it is.”). Living significance concerns realized living content; 生生 is the object of the ethical direction, compared by widening, and the `living` readings, which all read “not damaging”, do not include further generation. Ren's proposal of 10 October 2026, that “it can be anything that want's its continuation to have significance” and that “the whole … is actually perspective dependent” ([source](·)), was first analysed as putting a center at every wanting point; since centers and boundaries form within the dynamics and along dependence the center is not derived, the condition is read as its wording says (§6.4), and self-significance (reading “wanting one's continuation”) and standpoint neutrality follow from it. Living on, descent and conveyance are adopted as formed relations of continuation, not direct valuations. The weak form, for each formation, that its undamaging continuation has significance, reads “as long as not harm” as retaining (§6.4), the deontic reading (a claim on others not to harm) being unformalized; the strong form, for the whole, that continuation creates more significance, reads “more” as widening and can be met only where the world stays open (§1.3). The earlier reading, its draft restatement and the narration of D11–D15 are kept in the history of the chapter as of 17 October 2026.
