-### 6.8 What the continuation condition yields
-
-After proposing the condition, Ren answered that a center and its boundary exist only within cognitive structure and dynamics, formed within the same system. So there is no question of whose continuation matters that would need an axiom to settle it, and a center can be modelled as a thing like everything else. Ren also answered that “not harm” is a phase transition with a clear boundary ([words](·)). Following that answer, the condition is not read as putting a center at every wanting point (section 6.7). It is read as Ren's words themselves: for anything, its continuation into the future has significance. The checked content follows ([Becoming.Significance](·), [study section 53](·)). Each theorem below that is said to hold “under the condition” takes `Unrestricted` as a hypothesis; the others hold for any significance.
-
-- **The condition as a proposition.** A significance says, for a standpoint, a step and a formation, whether from that standpoint the formation's continuation at that step has significance. The condition, `Unrestricted`, says that nothing restricts it: from every standpoint the continuation of anything has significance at every step. It is boundary neutrality (`Neutral`, section 6.2) applied once, to the significance of continuation; as a predicate it is the one that holds everywhere. A rival keeps the same rule inside each standpoint's region (`bounded_rival`).
-- **Under the condition, living significance follows immediately** ([one-axiom-yields-g0](·)). Take any reading in which a claim's significance from a standpoint is the significance of some formation's continuation at some step. Under the condition, living significance holds at the level of claims, and so do self-significance at every standpoint, relational neutrality, standpoint neutrality and, wherever something lives, a seed, with no connection used (`Valuation.premises_of_unrestricted`). The stepwise, relation-level and whole-run readings are such readings (`Web.significant_of_unrestricted`, `Conditions.significant_of_unrestricted`). The step is an instantiation: living significance is the condition restricted to living claims. What the condition gives is significance for every claim, living or not, and for formations not yet formed; it gives no positive valence, and `living` includes no further generation. On the level paths of a web (`Web.paths`), under the condition, living significance holds with positive significance read as significance from every standpoint, and so does C with “better” read as retaining and adding what has significance (`Web.paths_g0_comparison`). So under the condition the premise card's seed, self-significance, relational neutrality, standpoint neutrality and, on level paths, C hold. A, L and the practical commitments remain premises.
-- **What has significance is what can form** ([significance-retained-within-margin](·)). From a standpoint, one level path *retains* what has significance along another when it admits every continuation with significance that the other admits (`Web.Retains`). It *adds* when it admits one that the other does not (`Web.Adds`). Under the condition, retaining is inclusion and adding is exceeding (`Web.retains_iff_includes`, `Web.adds_iff_exceeds`), alike from every standpoint (`Web.retains_agree`). So, under the condition, the four cases of a part (section 2) are the four cases of significance, and Ren's strong form, to “create more significance”, is the generative case of the weak form, with no further condition.
-- **Not harm is an exact boundary, for any significance.** In a balanced flow, compared at the levels with the part withheld, the levels with a part retain what has significance without it exactly when, for every continuation with significance that the levels without it admit, the part's net draw stays within the margin (`Flow.Balances.retains_iff_within_margin`). The part loses a continuation with significance exactly where its net draw exceeds the margin (`Flow.Balances.loses_iff_beyond_margin`). It adds one exactly where its net exchange brings within the margin a formation that the levels without it do not admit (`Flow.Balances.adds_iff_within_margin`). These laws take no condition: the condition only fixes which continuations count. Reading them as Ren's “a phase transition with a clear boundary” is the AI's: the boundary is fixed by the part's own net exchange, with no will or belief from outside the dynamics.
-- **What has not yet formed counts.** In `Preemption` a drawer takes a condition's unit before any dependence on it forms. Its event is active and not undermining, so it is living on the stepwise reading. Yet its part narrows what can form: a formation requiring the condition from the next step on is admitted at every step without the part, and at no later step with it. Under the condition, the part loses a continuation with significance (`Preemption.not_undermining_yet_loses`). The stepwise reading counts only dependences that have been met; retaining also counts what can still form. The two readings of not harm differ, and not harm reads as retaining [AI reading, D13].
-- **No ending is licensed.** A level path that retains what has significance along another ends none of it (`Web.Retains.not_added`). Under the condition, the conveyor's part is unordered, each path adding what the other lacks (`Transfer.unordered`), so ordering it needs a measure, which is a further premise. Under the condition, the giver's part retains and adds (`Restoring.Inflow.retains_adds`).
-- **The whole first** ([whole-first-and-bounded-centers](·)). The fewer continuations have significance, the more is retained (`Web.Retains.of_fewer`); significance bounded by a region retains what is admitted within the region (`Web.retains_bounded_iff`). Under the condition, what retains in the whole retains within every region, a system's or a self's (`Web.Retains.within`). What holds within a system holds within every region inside it (`Web.AdmitsWithin.narrow`). The converse fails. In `Clearing`, let each formation's significance stop at what its continuation depends on. From the clearer's standpoint its part retains what has significance at every step; from the dweller's standpoint it loses the dweller (`Clearing.centers_disagree`). Under the condition the part loses the dweller from every standpoint, while the levels without it admit every formation at every step and the clearer is supported throughout, so withholding the part ends nothing (`Clearing.free_rider_loses`). This gives Ren's order of levels, the whole, then the system one is in, then the self, as an order of how complete a judgment is, not as a description of what life does [AI reading, D43].
-- **The represented dynamics do not entail significance.** Where nothing has significance, every level path retains every other, none adds, and living significance fails at any event that lives; where everything has significance, it holds (`Web.significance_undetermined`). The theorem compares the significance that holds everywhere with the one that holds nowhere, a free parameter not built from `World` data. It shows that the represented dynamics, which contain no significance, do not entail it; it is not evidence that becoming leaves significance undetermined. A significance bounded by a region is supplied as the condition is. Ren wrote that the self “can not justify itself without some sort of "belief"”; here that reads as: a significance bounded by the self is a premise too.
-
-**Reading Ren's words.** `Unrestricted` reads Ren's proposed condition: the formation index reads “anything”, a formation's continuation at a step reads “its continuation into the future”, and the standpoint index reads “has significance” without qualification, no center being privileged. Significance is not graded and, as Ren wrote, need not be positive. Retaining reads “as long as not harm”: a part does no harm where the levels with it retain what has significance without it. Adding reads “create more significance” and “more possibilities of becoming”: a part that also adds is generative. Under the condition, the reading of section 6.7, self-significance as wanting and standpoint neutrality for the center, is a consequence: the condition gives self-significance at every standpoint and standpoint neutrality.
-
-**What this does not derive.** The step from significance to a reason (A), the lifting (L) and practical judgment (the practical commitments); a measure that orders mixed parts; the level at which formations are individuated (members or lineages), which fixes what counts as a loss; which reading the `living` of living significance names (`Preemption` shows that two readings differ); and the normative warrant of the condition itself. Recognition and motivation belong to the route without axiom (section 6.9). In `Clearing.centers_disagree`, a center whose represented boundary is exactly its actual dependence still licenses the free rider; section 6.9 shows that without the condition the loss registers only where the dependence reaches what is closed. With the condition as a hypothesis, living significance is a theorem, immediate at the level of claims, and through the laws without axiom not harm and generativity have exact forms. Living significance itself is not an axiom (sections 5 and 6.12).
