-### 6.11 The condition decomposed: the self's presupposition and the step of invariance
-
-In “Truth exist” Ren wrote: “There is a set of universal invariations, that for every universe, becoming happens, the law follows”, that it is “the bases of all ethics, for all beings, in all universes”, and “There is no absolute self, and the continuation goes beyond one’s cycle of life, goes beyond one’s death.” ([source](·)). Earlier Ren had written that the self is “a cognitive model which can not justify itself without some sort of "belief"”, that “we” are “the universe/ecosystem that realizes its own existence” ([source](·)), and that a center's “boundary” “is also with in the same cognitive system” ([source](·)).
-
-The AI proposed, in its own words ([source](·)), that the condition does not follow from the dynamics but may follow from three claims: every act presupposes that some continuation matters; there is no absolute self; truth is the same for every being. The one step a critic must deny is the move from “the continuation I act for” to “continuation as such”. The AI proposed stating that step exactly, checking its skeleton in Lean and having it independently attacked. The three claims are the AI's reading of Ren's words, not claims shown to be Ren's own. Ren answered: “continue, let's pursue the strongest claims and complete proof”.
-
-This section states the result ([Becoming.Boundaries](·), [study section 62](·)). It is an exact decomposition of the condition that locates the step and does not lower the condition's content. Logically it is the identity A ⇔ P ∧ (P → A), given that A implies P, with supervaluation bookkeeping for P: it locates the contested step and derives nothing beyond it. The theory asserts neither side.
-
-- **Boundaries of a self; super-truth and sub-truth** ([presupposition-scopes](·)). Along a relation, a boundary of a formation's self is a region that holds the formation and is closed under the relation (`Boundary`). The closure is the least boundary and the whole the greatest (`Boundary.closure`, `Boundary.whole`); where everything lies within the formation's closure, the whole is its only boundary (`Boundary.only_whole`). A claim about a self is *super-true* when it holds however the boundary is drawn among the admissible ones (`SuperTrue`), *sub-true* when it holds as the boundary is drawn somewhere (`SubTrue`), and *boundary-invariant* when, holding as drawn anywhere, it holds as drawn everywhere (`BoundaryInvariant`). The first two terms are those of supervaluation (Fine 1975) and subvaluation (Hyde 1997). Super-truth is invariant sub-truth (`superTrue_iff`), and invariance is determinacy: if sub-true, the claim is super-true (`boundaryInvariant_iff_determinate`). What lies within the self however its boundary is drawn is exactly the closure, while everything lies within it as drawn somewhere (`superTrue_member_iff`, `subTrue_member`): along a relation, no formation is a clear non-member of any self.
-- **The presupposition and its two scopes.** From a standpoint, with the boundary drawn at a region, the presupposition is that the continuation of everything within the region has significance (`SignificantWithin`). Super-true, it is significance over the union of the admissible boundaries; where the whole is admissible, as along any relation, it is the condition at that standpoint, whatever the relation (`superTrue_significantWithin_iff_union`, `unrestricted_iff_superTrue`, `superTrue_level_free`). Sub-true along a relation, it is significance over the closure (`subTrue_significantWithin_iff`). Along the empty relation that is the significance of the center's own continuation, a standpoint's own good; along the total relation it is the condition at that standpoint (`subTrue_empty_iff`, `subTrue_total_iff`); along a larger relation it says more (`subTrue_of_larger`). Route (b)'s significance, bounded by each center's closure, is the significance of what lies definitely within the self, and the least significance that makes every presupposition sub-true (`bounded_closure_iff`, `bounded_closure_least`). So route (b) and the condition are one presupposition, with the operator “however the boundary is drawn” at narrow scope and at wide scope (`presupposition_scopes`); the operator does not distribute over the conditional. This extends route (b) from feeding to any relation.
-- **The condition decomposed: where its content lies** ([axiom-decomposition](·)). Let every formation lie within some admissible boundary of every self (covering), let each standpoint's presupposition be sub-true, and let it be boundary-invariant. Then nothing restricts significance (`unrestricted_of_presupposed`). Where the whole is an admissible boundary of every self, the condition is exactly the presupposition sub-true and invariant at every standpoint (`unrestricted_iff_presupposed`); along any relation the whole is admissible, so there it is exactly that (`unrestricted_iff_presupposed_along`). Wherever the whole is admissible, invariance is the conditional from the presupposition to the condition at that standpoint (`boundaryInvariant_iff_conditional`); given the presupposition, invariance is the condition there (`boundaryInvariant_iff_all`), which section 6.8 reads as boundary neutrality. So the decomposition locates the step and does not lower the condition's content. The step runs both ways: where some continuation lacks significance, an invariant presupposition is nowhere true (`not_subTrue_of_invariant`). Along a relation, covering holds by construction, because every closed region holding the center, the whole included, counts as an admissible drawing of the self. Given the presupposition at every standpoint, and every formation within some center's closure, boundary-invariance is equivalent to standpoint-invariance (`StandpointInvariant`, `boundaryInvariant_iff_standpointInvariant`), the rule of standpoint neutrality; without the presupposition everywhere the two come apart (`OneCounts.forms_apart`). So these premises carry two decompositions already in the core over to the significance of continuation: `Valuation.significant_iff` (a seed and both neutralities on a connected whole) and `Valuation.significant_iff_held` (self-significance at every standpoint with standpoint neutrality). Agreement between standpoints and living significance at the level of claims follow from them (`retains_agree_of_presupposed`, `Valuation.significant_of_presupposed`).
-- **Each premise is needed.** In `Clearing`, where nothing has significance, the presupposition is invariant and the whole is admissible, and the condition fails (`Clearing.without_presupposition`). Significance bounded by each formation's feeding closure makes every presupposition sub-true with the whole admissible, and the condition fails; at the clearer the presupposition is not boundary-invariant, and significance is not standpoint-invariant (`Clearing.without_invariance`, `Clearing.without_standpoint_invariance`). If each self's only admissible boundary were its feeding closure, the same significance would make every presupposition sub-true and invariant, the dweller would lie within no admissible boundary of the clearer, and the condition would still fail (`Clearing.with_fixed_boundary`).
-- **A part within reach.** Sub-true along a relation that holds affecting, the presupposition compares every part within the center's closure as the condition does (`Flow.Balances.presupposed_comparison`): along affecting, every part within the center's reach closure (`Flow.Balances.presupposed_reach_comparison`); along sharing a condition, every part within its system. Neither invariance nor super-truth is used. Sub-truth along sharing a condition gives sub-truth along affecting (`Flow.presupposition_order`), so the premise along affecting is the weaker. Sub-truth depends on the relation and super-truth does not (`Clearing.levels_differ`). Drawn along sharing a condition, or held however the boundary is drawn, the clearer's own presupposition gives, from its own standpoint, that its part loses the dweller; drawn at the feeding closure, it is met by a significance under which the part retains (`Clearing.own_presupposition`). These are corollaries of the comparison of section 6.10 ([comparison-within-reach](·)).
-- **Where the closure is the whole.** Where every formation lies within each center's closure along a relation, the whole is the only boundary, so invariance holds trivially and the condition is the presupposition sub-true at every standpoint (`unrestricted_iff_presupposed_of_whole`). Along sharing a condition this holds wherever one condition is taken part in by everything (`Flow.unrestricted_iff_system_presupposed`, `Flow.unrestricted_iff_presupposed_of_common`), as in `Clearing` (`Clearing.system_presupposition`). The step is not removed there: it has moved into drawing the self's boundary closed under the relation.
-
-**Reading.**
-- The presupposition reads the “belief” without which, Ren wrote, the self “can not justify itself”. Ren wrote this of the self's limit. Using the belief as a premise is the AI's step, and sub-truth along a relation is far stronger than that some continuation has significance.
-- Covering: Ren's “we” being “the universe/ecosystem that realizes its own existence” supports the whole as one drawing of “we”; “There is no absolute self” does not by itself give covering. Along a relation covering holds because every closed region holding the center, the whole included, counts as an admissible drawing of the self. That admissibility is the substantive choice, and it is why the admissible class is not a supervaluation of the ordinary, vague “self”: it has no clear non-members.
-- Ren's “for all beings” reads most directly as standpoint-invariance, the rule of standpoint neutrality; given the presupposition and covering, boundary-invariance is equivalent to it. Ren's “universal invariations” are invariances of the law across universes; extending them to significance is the AI's reading. To deny the step is to hold the presupposition true only relative to a drawing or only from a standpoint, or, since the step runs both ways, to give up the presupposition. The step takes the place of the earlier route's tolerance ([review](·)) and, like tolerance with Chain, carries all of the condition's content beyond the presupposition, in one step instead of many small ones. Arguments from an agent's standpoint to impartial ethics are contested at exactly this step: agent-relative against agent-neutral reasons (Nagel 1970), and Gewirth's Principle of Generic Consistency (1978) with its critics. Parfit (1984) read the absence of a deep self as weakening the privilege of the self-interest theory, which corresponds here to covering. Nor does the step dissolve what Sidgwick called the dualism of practical reason; it locates that dualism in this step. This placement among the literature is argued, not formal.
-- Where the rivals sit. Along a relation, covering holds by construction, so the rivals deny another premise. A rival that grounds significance in a formed closure denies sub-truth along any relation under which that closure is not closed, as operational closure is not closed under feeding. Along a relation under which it is closed, it denies invariance: it holds its presupposition only at that closure, as route (b) does at the feeding closure. It denies covering only if it also restricts the admissible drawings to that closure. A vague self denies covering where every admissible drawing leaves the stranger out, and invariance where the stranger is borderline. A graded weight that falls to zero denies sub-truth if it falls inside the closure, and invariance if beyond it. A present-aim evaluator denies sub-truth. The first two bear in the same way on the earlier tolerance route to living significance. This section locates these denials; it does not refute them.
-- Ren's order of levels, “the whole, and a weaker version is within the system that one is in, then the self”, is an order of readings of the presupposition: super-true; sub-true along affecting, at the reach closure offered in section 6.10 for the system one is in; and sub-true at the self, along the empty relation. The weaker version gives the condition's comparison on every part within one's reach. The reach closure points forward: on this reading the order runs down to the bare self, not through the feeding closure, which lies on another branch (`Flow.presupposition_order`) [AI reading, D21].
-
-**What this does not derive.** Covering, sub-truth and invariance themselves: the presupposition is supplied as every significance is (`Web.significance_undetermined`), and along a relation it already carries transmission along that relation, from the bare own good of the empty relation to the condition of the total one. That a center knows its reach closure, since its own feedback registers at most its influence closure (`Flow.Balances.uncoupled_beyond_influence`). The step from significance to a reason, to motivation or to practice. Living significance is not an axiom: the audit of its uses is clean (section 6.12).
