+### 6.5 Scope and order: the step of invariance, C and practical judgment
+
+**In words.** The ethics rests on two premises with two roles. The continuation condition fixes scope: exactly decomposed, it is the self's presupposition (from a standpoint, the continuation of what lies within its boundary has significance) joined to the step of invariance (that presupposition does not change with how the self's boundary is drawn). That step is the condition's content beyond the self; it extends the scope to losses that return to no one, and it ranks nothing. C, the widening comparison, fixes order: calling widening better is the only premise that ranks courses. Courses are compared on possibilities; lifting (L) and the practical commitments (J1–J4) carry the comparison to responses and choice. Neither premise is asserted, and no ethical result follows from the condition alone.
+
+- `unrestricted_iff_presupposed_along`: along any relation the whole is an admissible boundary of every self, and the condition is exactly the presupposition sub-true (holding as the boundary is drawn somewhere, `SubTrue`) and boundary-invariant (`BoundaryInvariant`) at every standpoint; generally where the whole is admissible (`unrestricted_iff_presupposed`), and from covering (`unrestricted_of_presupposed`). Super-truth (`SuperTrue`, after Fine 1975; sub-truth after Hyde 1997) is invariant sub-truth (`superTrue_iff`), and what lies within the self however its boundary is drawn is exactly the closure (`superTrue_member_iff`). Logically the decomposition is A ⇔ P ∧ (P → A), given A ⇒ P, with supervaluation bookkeeping: it locates the contested step and derives nothing beyond it. The step runs both ways (`not_subTrue_of_invariant`); where the whole is admissible it is the conditional from the presupposition to the condition (`boundaryInvariant_iff_conditional`); given the presupposition everywhere and every formation within some closure it is standpoint-invariance, the rule of standpoint neutrality (`boundaryInvariant_iff_standpointInvariant`; apart otherwise, `OneCounts.forms_apart`).
+- `presupposition_scopes`: route (b) and the condition are one presupposition with “however the boundary is drawn” at narrow and wide scope. Sub-true along a relation, it is significance over the closure (`subTrue_significantWithin_iff`): along the empty relation a standpoint's own good, along the total relation the condition (`subTrue_empty_iff`, `subTrue_total_iff`); route (b)'s significance is the least making every presupposition sub-true (`bounded_closure_least`). Sub-true along affecting it compares every part within the reach closure as the condition does, using neither invariance nor super-truth (`Flow.Balances.presupposed_reach_comparison`; along sharing, the system, which is the stronger premise, `Flow.presupposition_order`). Where every formation lies within each closure, invariance is trivial and the step has moved into drawing the self's boundary closed under the relation (`unrestricted_iff_presupposed_of_whole`, `Flow.unrestricted_iff_presupposed_of_common`). Each premise is needed (`Clearing.without_presupposition`, `Clearing.without_invariance`, `Clearing.with_fixed_boundary`).
+- `forced_iff_center`: taken across standpoints from each standpoint's presupposition about its own continuation alone, the step forces significance for exactly the standpoints' centers (`atCenters_least`), and gives the condition only where every formation is a center (`unrestricted_atCenters_iff`); taken across drawings it needs no other standpoint (`boundaryInvariant_iff_all`). What a standpoint's own presupposition forces is exactly its closure (`forced_iff_within`). Order has the same shape: one course widens another exactly when every weighting that counts every formation ranks it higher, however partially it weighs (`Weighting.widens_iff_every_positive`, on webs `Web.widens_iff_every_weighting`), and the same holds for every order that ranks each widening higher, additive or not, priority to the worse off and lexical priority included (`Weighting.widens_iff_every_of_class`, `Weighting.widens_iff_every_score`, `Weighting.increasing_prior`, `Weighting.increasing_lexical`), so partiality decides exactly the mixed comparisons, either way (`Weighting.mixed_either_way`), a weight of zero denies scope (`Weighting.weighed_eq_of_unweighted`) and one weight for every formation counts numbers (`Weighting.neutral_ranks_by_number`). The mathematics of the last is Sen's intersection approach. The argument for the step, the literature that already has it (Gewirth; Parfit and Siderits) and each objection of §8.9 are in [THE-STEP-OF-INVARIANCE](·).
+- `Ranking.possible_extends_iff`: C read on possibilities, including a formation wherever a course's levels admit it, is under the condition retaining and adding what has significance. It ranks the absence of an overdrawing formation above its occurrence, restraint above overdraw, also with a third formation, and sharing above overdraw by consumption (`Ranking.possible_ranks`, `Ranking.possible_restraint`, `Ranking.ThirdParty.possible_extends`, `Ranking.possible_contest`), withholding no event (`Ranking.malignant_possible`), and a course nowhere lower is never ranked below (`Web.not_added_of_le`). It leaves unranked a formation drawing within renewal, which adds no possibility (`Ranking.possible_tie`): the value of bringing new lives into existence, not treated. Possibilities first, then a reading, would rank it but also rank a pause that adds no possibility below uninterrupted activity (`Ranking.Pause.pause_ranked_below`), a further premise. Under the whole-run reading restraint is ranked above overdraw for any number of drawers: taking no more and giving no less from levels as high eases the course, so the restrained course extends the other exactly when it includes an event the other withholds (`Ranking.restraint_extends_iff`, `Flow.Balances.eases_of_restrained`; `TwoDrawers.restraint_ranks`); under the stepwise reading easing withdraws exactly the events the easing course undermines, and a course whose levels never fall undermines nothing, so the same holds where moreover the restrained flow takes from no condition more than it gives (`Ranking.stepwise_extends_iff_of_eases`, `Ranking.restraint_extends_iff_stepwise`, ST1, [study §315](·), [the stepwise law of easing](·)); taking no more alone does not suffice (`Ranking.ThirdParty.stepwise_not_monotone`). The relation-level reading, whose claims are a formation's relations to conditions (`Ranking.relational`, the `living` of `Web.relations`), withdraws under easing exactly the relations the easing course no longer takes part in or undermines, so restraint that also keeps taking part, drawing less rather than nothing, is ranked above overdraw under it too (`Ranking.relational_extends_iff_of_eases`, `Ranking.restraint_extends_iff_relational`, RL1, [study §318](·), [the relation-level law of easing](·)); in the two-part family it leaves absence and occurrence unranked, as the stepwise reading does (`Ranking.relational_unranked`). The priority of basic conditions recovers the ranking step by step: read with the sustaining formation's events as the basic tier and the focal formation's as gains, the course without the malignant formation keeps every basic claim and one the other loses, so every comparison meeting J1 ranks absence above malignant growth under both readings (`Ranking.basic_first_stepwise`, `Ranking.basic_first_ranks`, J1S, [study §320](·), [the priority of basic conditions step by step](·)).
+- `articulation_iff_lifted`: comparing responses with several outcomes needs a lifting rule, and under the conservative L (“every outcome is better than every outcome”) the comparison, the reason, the survival of coordinated choice and continual improvement having no survivor hold on every frame, the functional situation being exactly the deterministic case. L is substantive: a response with one good and one bad outcome is incomparable both ways, and transitivity needs a feasible intermediate response.
+- `Direction.chosen_keeps_basic`: under J1/J2 (“basic conditions first, then living gain”, `Lexical.Frame.Above`; on a frame's steps `FrontierFrames.Priority`, the options being what one move reaches), a chosen move keeps the basic admissions some move keeps, and with options listed and comparisons decided the keeping is required (`FrontierFrames.Priority.kept_required`, `Direction.kept_required`); a choice at every step needs weak excluded middle (`FrontierFrames.choice_exists_iff_weakly`). On a world J3's joint plan at a step is the move, and a sole giver to what a formation requires is required and active (`FrontierWorlds.sole_giver_required`, `FrontierWorlds.sole_giver_active`, `FrontierWorlds.Discharged.no_residual`). Used in §7.5.
+
+Under the condition, A read with bare significance gives a reason for any new content, living or not (`BareSignificance.bare_forces_reason`), so A must be read on living content (`articulates_total`), and then the universal reason follows with no seed, neutrality or connection premise (`universal_reason_of_unrestricted`); A remains a premise, itself a neutrality premise. What C ranks under a reading of `living` (`Becoming.Ranking`): a continuation without a formation extends the one with it only if the reading withholds every event of that formation; under the whole-run reading the absence of an overdrawing formation ranks higher, under the stepwise reading an event at whose step every need is met is included and C no longer decides (malignant growth and overdraw by consumption are instances; `Immediate` where support is overstepped at once); restraint ranks above overdraw under both readings (`Ranking.restraint_ranks`, `Ranking.malignant_restraint`) and can be lost with a third party (`ThirdParty`). FR, finite responsiveness, is an additional, revisable comparison commitment, neither theorem nor axiom, whose formal content is `Becoming.LossMatching`. Other named commitments of the practical line are stated in their chapters with their records, each additional and revisable: BC1, BC2, LC, LR and CP in [basic conflict judgment](·), NP in [choice and generative context](·).
+
+**What it does not do.** It proves none of self-significance, relational neutrality, standpoint neutrality, A, C, L or the practical commitments, binds no position that rejects them, and does not treat the value of bringing new lives into existence. Normative warrant, recognition, motivation, compliance and actual preservation are different claims; so are direction, continuing capacity, per-step monotonic growth and scalar maximization. Covering, sub-truth and invariance are supplied as every significance is (§5); along a relation the presupposition already carries transmission along it, from the bare own good of the empty relation to the condition of the total one.
+
+*Readings* [AI reading, D1, D16, D21]. In “Truth exist” Ren wrote: “There is a set of universal invariations, that for every universe, becoming happens, the law follows”, that it is “the bases of all ethics, for all beings, in all universes”, and “There is no absolute self, and the continuation goes beyond one’s cycle of life, goes beyond one’s death.” ([source](·)); earlier, that the self is “a cognitive model which can not justify itself without some sort of "belief"” ([source](·)) and that a center's “boundary” “is also with in the same cognitive system” ([source](·)). The AI proposed that the condition may follow from three claims, every act presupposing that some continuation matters, no absolute self, and truth the same for every being, the one step a critic must deny being from “the continuation I act for” to “continuation as such” ([source](·)); the three claims are the AI's reading, not shown to be Ren's. The presupposition reads the self's “belief”, which Ren wrote of the self's limit, using it as a premise being the AI's step; covering is supported by the whole as one drawing of “we”, while “There is no absolute self” does not by itself give it, and admitting every closed region as a drawing is the substantive choice, so the admissible class is not a supervaluation of the ordinary, vague “self”. “For all beings” reads most directly as standpoint-invariance, and extending “universal invariations” from laws to significance is the AI's reading. To deny the step is to hold the presupposition only relative to a drawing or a standpoint, or to give it up. The step replaces the earlier route's tolerance ([review](·)) and is where arguments from an agent's standpoint to impartial ethics are contested: agent-relative against agent-neutral reasons (Nagel 1970), Gewirth's Principle of Generic Consistency (1978) and its critics, Parfit (1984) on the self-interest theory, corresponding here to covering; Sidgwick's dualism is located in this step, not dissolved; this placement is argued, not formal. The rivals sit at different premises: a rival grounding significance in a formed closure denies sub-truth along relations under which the closure is not closed, as operational closure is not closed under feeding, and invariance along those under which it is; a vague self denies covering or invariance; a graded weight falling to zero denies sub-truth inside the closure and invariance beyond; a present-aim evaluator denies sub-truth; this locates the denials and refutes none. Ren's order of levels is an order of readings of the presupposition: super-true; sub-true along affecting, at the reach closure; sub-true at the self; the reach closure points forward, so the order runs down to the bare self, not through the feeding closure. Courses are compared on possibilities [AI reading, D1] because (1) under the condition extension is retaining and adding with no further premise (conditional only); (2) it is the comparison of the generative space, being generative being that a part's “existence creates more possibilities of becoming”; (3) it ranks the absence of an overdrawing formation, restraint and sharing higher while withholding no event; (4) rest and restraint are never worse. The AI once read living content as 生生, and D1's revision withdrew it. A stronger argument for another comparison would revise this reading.
+
