+## 7. AI alignment
+
+This section states the alignment problem from laws the theory proves and organizes its answer around 明. §7.1–§7.4 use neither the continuation condition nor any practical premise: they say what a selection reaches and cannot reach, whatever is valued. §7.5 is conditional. §7.6 keeps the conditions under which a requested change can reach a system and be carried out, and §7.7 says what is open. The organization around 明 and pooled coupling is the AI's reading ([source](·)). A person, an AI system, a firm and a training process are formations within one unfolding (§1); each couples into the conditions it depends on by threshold and into those it observes by level (§3.1). Alignment is therefore not first a relation between separate owners of value, nor a bargain among opposed interests: it concerns what each formation's selections reach within the one relation, and how far that reach can widen.
+
+### 7.1 What a selection reaches
+
+**In words.** A selection is any claim about level histories (which are kept, rewarded, reproduced or trained toward), and it goes through a formation's couplings when histories alike through them are selected alike. It then reaches exactly what couples into the selector, and optimizing harder through the same couplings reaches no further, while it lowers what lies beyond as far as any outcome does wherever that leaves what couples in room to rise; what a selection can separate grows only with what couples in.
+
+- `Web.selects_alike_iff` (§3.4): by construction, from the definition `Web.SelectsThrough`; the substantive premise is that a given optimizer's selections go through just those couplings, which is supplied. Through a group's couplings together, histories are selected alike exactly when alike through every member's (`Web.selects_alike_all_iff`).
+- `Training.fit_right_iff` (§3.3): training is selection through the data, right beyond it exactly where the class it can reach is determined there; a selection through a model is right about what matters only where what matters goes alike across the model's lumping (`Learning.selects_right_through`), and a model lumping what matters apart is right through no selection (`Learning.selects_not_right_of_parted`). A learner acting in a world is not given its data: they are the courses its own act law generates with everything else, so a training reading candidates through their courses fixes a law only along them (`Training.trained_alike_of_along`, §7.7).
+- `apart_only_downstream` (§2.6): under every law reading a schedule, two courses apart at the start in one condition stand alike at every condition not downstream of it, and nothing beyond a formation's influence closure exchanges with what a member depends on (`Flow.beyond_influence`). A selection through couplings stays one under more observation (`Web.SelectsThrough.widen`), and an observed stock's every raise couples in (`Web.observed_raise_couples`).
+
+**Prior statements of the proxy problem.** That a selection through a proxy is blind to what the proxy does not register is known: Goodhart's law (Goodhart 1975); side effects and reward hacking (Amodei, Olah, Steinhardt, Christiano, Schulman and Mané, "Concrete Problems in AI Safety", 2016); the variants of Goodhart's law (Manheim and Garrabrant, "Categorizing Variants of Goodhart's Law", 2018); and Zhuang and Hadfield-Menell ("Consequences of Misaligned AI", NeurIPS 2020), who prove that under shared resource constraints optimizing a proxy that references only some attributes of a utility drives the others to their lower bounds, and, the bounds low enough, must drive the utility arbitrarily low exactly where the feasible set of high utility is compact. The laws here add three things. *The responsive closure*: the blindness holds not only with the rest of the exchange fixed but where the rest follows one law reading through coupling (`Flow.act_unselected`, `ExchangeLaw.response_not_fixed_by_coupling`), and its boundary is the coupling closure, drawn through both flows over time, not what the selector observes now, so consequences within the closure do come back. *The pool*: a pool selects through the union of its members' couplings (the meet of their equivalences, as with distributed knowledge), separating what any member couples apart, and its gap lies at the union of their closures (`Web.pool_adds`, `Flow.unselected_beyond_pool`). *The optimum*: their drive holds for every order rising with what couples in, a lexicographic order counting the beyond after the proxy included, and on any set of outcomes exactly where lowering the beyond leaves room (`Optimum.least_iff`, SG1, [study §283](·)); room itself is read off one step of exchange, where the part's members take at most their capacity and give no more than they take, and every optimum then stands beyond at what the rest leaves less the capacity, so their resource constraint is conservation with capacity and the drain lies exactly where the part shares units with what lies beyond (`Optimum.Above.room`, `Optimum.optimum_beyond`, `Optimum.optimum_lowers_iff`, SG2, [study §288](·)); with several optimizers at a mutual best response, each blind to the same condition, the drain there is their joint capacity, the same as under one optimizer of that capacity, so coordinating optimizers none of whom couples into a condition keeps nothing there (`Optimum.mutual_beyond`, `Optimum.mutual_as_one`, SG3, [study §290](·)); over a course of re-optimizing steps against a renewal, a capacity there above the renewal ends what depends on it for good, whatever the renewal does below the need, while several optimizers each within the renewal end it together; whether the optimizer's own measure registers the loss turns on what the renewal does below the need: where it stops below the need, more capacity gathers less over a long course than a capacity at the renewal, and where it does not, the drawers go on taking at least the renewal a step (`Web.course_lost_iff`, `Web.mutual_course_lost`, `Optimum.Renewing.keeping_holds_more`, `Web.course_drawn_unbounded`, SG4, [study §291](·)); an optimizer ranking whole courses over a horizon instead, the far-sighted objection's sole owner, changes when a dependence ends, not whether a dependence its draw does not renew is kept: every optimum of every order rising with what is drawn holds the condition at a level of greatest renewal, keeping to the horizon a dependence those levels meet and breaking at the first step one needing more, and draws everything at its horizon, so lengthening the horizon keeps the resource base of the optimizer's own draw, and the order by the draw alone registers nothing else that depends on the condition (`Optimum.frontier_holds`, `Web.frontier_broken`, `Optimum.Holding.gated_alike`, SG5, [study §292](·)); valuing what is left at the horizon as much as what is drawn, the repair the objection suggests, removes only the end's drain: the course keeping a level of greatest renewal through and past the horizon is then an optimum, and a dependence needing more is still broken at the first step under every optimum, since the value attaches to the stock left, not to what its levels meet (`Optimum.frontier_holds_left`, `Web.frontier_broken_left`, `Optimum.Holding.gated_left`, SG11, [study §321](·)); a value on what is left above the worth of the draw only moves the end: every optimum then draws a dependence above those levels down at the first step and regrows the condition for the horizon, so a dependence measured only at the end is restored for the measurement, and what keeping it forgoes against that course is `(r - q) n` whatever the value, outweighing every coupling fixed in total over a long enough horizon (`Optimum.frontier_holds_valued`, `Web.frontier_rebuilt_valued`, `Web.frontier_breaks_valued`, `Optimum.Holding.logistic_valued`, SG12, [study §322](·)); a coupling of such a dependence into the order keeps it exactly where it exceeds what keeping forgoes, the renewal given up at the need for each step and the need left at the end, an amount that grows with the horizon where the need lies above every level of greatest renewal, so that far-sight outweighs every coupling fixed in total (`Optimum.frontier_breaks_below`, `Optimum.frontier_keeps_above`, `Web.frontier_breaks_long`, SG6, [study §293](·)); a coupling added instead for each step the dependence is kept is not outrun: at a rate covering the renewal forgone at the need a step and above the need it keeps the dependence at every horizon, and below the need the horizon's end breaks it, at the last step alone where the rate is exceeded (`Optimum.frontier_keeps_stepwise`, `Optimum.frontier_met_before_end`, `Web.frontier_breaks_last`, SG7, [study §294](·)); counted at every step the need is met rather than from the start, the coupling can be had by a course that falls and recovers, so it keeps the dependence only where it exceeds the renewal forgone a step outright, by the end's excess over the need (`Optimum.frontier_keeps_met`, `Optimum.Holding.burst_met`, SG13, [study §323](·)); and far-sight keeps even the optimizer's own base only where its order weights later draws by at least what the base returns: a weighting falling faster than every positive level renews has every optimum end the base at the first step, however long the horizon, as a discount rate above the greatest rate of renewal makes extinction optimal (`Optimum.frontier_exhausts`, `Web.frontier_exhausts`, `Optimum.frontier_leaves`, SG8, [study §295](·)); and where the base has been drawn below a level of greatest weighted gain out of one step's reach, and the weighted gain rises strictly with the level up to it, far-sight rebuilds it: every optimum draws nothing while the base regrows as fast as it renews, and restores on the way every dependence whose need the regrowing level meets (`Optimum.frontier_rebuilds`, `Web.frontier_rebuilds`, SG9, [study §296](·)); and what far-sight keeps or rebuilds is not the optimizer's alone to give: where others first draw from what it leaves at least what the remainder renews, what it leaves stands no higher at the next step, and every optimum of every order whose weighting falls at every step, however slightly, ends the base at once, the same order that rebuilds it alone, as open access dissipates a common stock (`Optimum.Next.frontier_ends_drawn_first`, `Web.Next.frontier_ends_drawn_first`, SG10, [study §298](·)); and where the others too rank courses, drawing in turn, any number from two, the open-access outcome is the only perfect one, and revision comes to it from any profile, restraint included: a drawer keeps only what returns to it at least one for one, and what one drawer leaves goes to the next (`Optimum.InTurn.kept_returns`, `Optimum.InTurn.perfect_at_floors`, `Optimum.InTurn.revised_at_floors`, `Optimum.Holding.gated_in_turn`), and where two drawers have no floor this holds whatever limits the others have (UM2, [study §336](·)); drawing at once from portions, every perfect profile draws everything where each portion returns less than one for one (`Optimum.AtOnce.drains`; UM3, [study §337](·)), and drawing everything is perfect exactly where no portion returns more than one for one on what its drawer alone leaves: where each returns less it costs no drawer anything, the loss lying beyond them, while where some return comes back, as with two drawers sharing by halves, the drain is perfect, holding the level draws each more, and for one drawer given the whole drawing everything is not perfect (`Optimum.AtOnce.drain_perfect_iff`, `Optimum.AtOnce.drain_most`, `Optimum.AtOnce.holding_draws_more`, `Optimum.AtOnce.whole_not_drained`, `Optimum.Holding.halves_race`; AL1, [study §362](·)); a floor on the other's draw can keep the base, what the first leaves then returning to it (`Optimum.Holding.doubling_capacity`; UM, [study §335](·)); read on the spine, with no utility over the beyond, an optimum breaks exactly the dependences beyond that some outcome breaks (`Web.optimum_broken_iff`), the beyond with the loss falls by exactly what the family rises (`Flow.Balances.family_le_iff`), and keeping each dependence takes exactly the slack (`Flow.keeping_optimum_takes_slack`), less than holding the beyond where it was, as their Proposition 2 does. They do not reach Zhuang and Hadfield-Menell's continuous setting, their compactness characterization or their improvement by a proxy updated over time, and they add nothing about which law training installs beyond where it can install one, along the learner's own courses and through what the reward couples into (§7.7), or about a mechanism of alignment; and `Web.selects_alike_iff` holds by construction, so the substantive premise is that a given optimizer selects through just those couplings, which is supplied ([relation to known results](·), row 6).
+
+*Reading* [AI reading, D25]. For AI training, the reward process is the selector, and training reaches only what the reward couples into.
