-## The theory stated whole
-
-This section closes the theory without axiom. The organization is the AI's, following Ren's proposal “let's aim for the strongest claim without axiom, as the first part”. It states the whole in prose; the full catalogue of its declarations, with each theorem's name and conditions, is kept in the chapter's reference under “Declaration catalogue of the whole”.
-
-**What “no axiom” means here.** The theory uses no axiom, ethical or substantive. Every theorem it cites is checked in Lean, and every source declaration of the core has an empty axiom report: no `propext`, `Quot.sound` or `Classical.choice` (section 9). That is a constructive discipline, not an absence of premises. Every substantive premise enters as a hypothesis of the theorem that uses it, and stated so, “no axiom” by itself excludes nothing. What the theory adds is that the hypotheses are named and local, and that the premises of a world are shown independent. The representation brings commitments of its own. The declared ones are discrete steps, natural-number amounts and a shared step index, which is one global linear order of steps. The representation also builds in more: every condition is a natural-number stock; dependence is admission at a threshold (need at most level); change is exchange of quantity, with a rest relatum that absorbs any imbalance; there is a least unit, and dissipation loses at least one unit per uptake; and formations come from a type given in advance. That what is counted is decided is the condition of the laws that count or name a step (`Becoming.Decidedness`); where a counting law quantifies over decided activity of every relatum, that global decidability is a condition of the law, not yet a local one. The remarks between theorems, for example that whether a premise holds is empirical, are not Lean statements.
-
-**I. What holds of every unfolding and every law of change.** With no premise about the unfolding, the theory states the readings of one change (`change_readings`, which holds by definition), the identity of an amount over a stretch (`over_stretch`), comings and ceasings, with holding decided, keeping pace within a family's size (`keep_pace`), the tally as the whole law of counting for properties of the counts read step by step (`counting_laws`), and the laws of one step, each with its condition inside it. These laws are definitional or arithmetic, and they exclude no unfolding beyond what the representation excludes; they locate the claims about the whole rather than add dynamical content. Of every law of change, again with no premise and with “a list holds the configurations” written into each law that uses it: within finitely many configurations a law merges nothing exactly where every configuration returns (`Law.lossless_iff_returns`); a kept history never returns and needs openness; what does not return is exactly what a determined law draws in; and within finitely many configurations a run is a course into a return. Asked of every process, a run from every member of every family that keeps moving is exactly dependent choice (`runs_iff_selection`). It also states the normal forms of reorderings, listing once exactly where identity is decided (`listsOnce_iff_decided`), the parity obstruction to gluing contextual readings, with Specker's boxes, CHSH and the Mermin–Peres square as instances (`ParitySystem.glues_iff`), exact bounds for identifying a finite-state history (`Identification.bounded_agree`) and for learning it, typicality as counting of situations, and where the gain behind novelty comes from. The unity theorems (`World.unity`, `Contextual.world`) show that the representations encode one another, for instance that every world's balance is a run of exchange; they are results of encodability, not further facts about worlds.
-
-**II. What each premise adds.** Premises are hypotheses of conditional theorems, not laws. The eight premises of a world are independent: for each, a world meets the other seven and not it (`World.independent`). Under the 256 selections of them, the laws of counting are classified exactly (`World.counting_under`), with the activity of every relatum decided; over counted censuses the same laws hold with no decision procedure and for every property of the counts (`World.counting_under_counted`). With a census, embodiment, balance and dissipation, and every step from some step on enclosed, that the world comes to rest cannot be refuted (`World.rests_unrefuted_enclosed`); arising without end then needs openness (`World.arising_opens`); a step after which nothing arises, asked of every finite world meeting the eight premises with its activity decided, would give the limited principle of omniscience (`World.lpo_of_finite_ends`). These laws of rest rely on the natural-number unit. At a refining unit, if the refinement is not counted, rest fails. Counted as a giving, refinement is excluded by dissipation and enclosure wherever anything stands (`Flow.refinement_gives_nothing`), and rest then follows from the fixed-unit theorem. In a balanced flow the history of exchanges grows at every level change with no dissipation premise, and a finite, lossless, enclosed world can exchange without end (`Passing.passes`). Beyond these, the theory states what dependence and reserve, parts and regions, feeding, feedback and reach, registration and testing, experiment, runaway, seeking, mechanism and response add. It states how much difference arrives and how a carried difference grows: where the rest follows a law of what has stood and every condition is listed once, the most difference that can arrive is the carried amount, which is attained (`most_difference_arrives`); with, in addition, the same formations and strengths at every step, it is bounded by a polynomial exactly where no loop lies upstream (`gap_polynomial_iff_no_loop`). A return at least doubles what is carried, given natural-number strengths of at least one. Several of these laws depend on the integrality of natural-number amounts: rest, novelty needing gain, bounded parts forgetting, and frequency rather than strength setting runaway. With real levels, a bounded part can be new at every step.
-
-**III. Where the dynamics stop deciding.** The laws above do not decide whether actual unfoldings meet the premises, which is empirical; the step after which nothing arises; the order of mixed parts, which needs a measure; a formation's center; how others respond; where models, moves, laws, targets, descriptions, hypotheses and registrations come from; or how many states a situation has, which the situation supplies. They give no part significance: on any web with an event that lives, living significance holds where everything has significance and fails where nothing has (`Web.significance_undetermined`). The represented dynamics contain no significance, so they do not entail it.
-
-**IV. How evaluation holds for any significance (sections 5–6).** With no axiom, for any significance and any valuation: the content of living significance is exactly a seed with both boundary neutralities on a connected whole with a living claim (`Valuation.significant_iff`), and every premise of that characterization is needed. A part retains what has significance exactly within the margin of its net draw, and loses and adds at equally exact boundaries. A part is generative where the levels with it widen those without it. Any significance covering what a part reaches gives the comparison by inclusion. On level paths, C's extension is exactly widening; that holds by definition, and that widening is better is the open question of warrant. The continuation condition is the condition of section 6.15. Under it living significance is immediate: the condition gives significance to every claim, not a positive valence. Where the whole is admissible, the condition is exactly the self's presupposition, sub-true and boundary-invariant at every standpoint; the decomposition locates the contested step of invariance and derives nothing beyond it (section 6.11).
-
-**The deepest part.** The sharpest results map where each principle of classical reasoning enters a law of change. Asking of every finite world that arising recurs exactly when ceasing does is excluded middle (`World.law_iff_em`). Naming the end step for every finite world gives the limited principle of omniscience (`World.lpo_of_finite_ends`), and deciding vanishing as a rule is exactly that principle as a rule (`vanishDecision_iff_lpoRule`). A counterexample to the least registration exists exactly where a rule decides, of every Boolean sequence, whether it is false throughout: the weak limited principle as a rule (`not_through_sensitive_iff_rule`). Asked of every process, the refutability of passing tests is Markov's principle (`refutable_passes_iff_markov`), the origin law with a proposition as the gate is double-negation elimination (`Gated.origin_of_propositions_iff`), and runs from every member of every family that keeps moving are dependent choice (`runs_iff_selection`).
-
-**What this completeness is.** This is the completeness of a formal statement in the sense of the four checkable criteria of [plan section 9](·), not a proof of necessity. The theory aims at the strongest claim with no axiom; that it is the strongest has not been shown, and the formal questions still open are in section 8. The families of the spine meet through correspondence theorems, not by definition. In the [theorem-level measurement](·) of 17 October 2026, after the join modules of board item U, 195 of 7,698 spine theorems stand apart from both base families (1,019 of 7,214 the day before), and each of the 134 roots among them stands apart for a stated reason: a support lemma, a statement of logical strength alone, a fact about one constructed model, a restatement, a law of every valuation on any type, or a bridge interface. The laws hold of worlds so represented. Whether every becoming can be so represented is part of the warrant still needed (section 8).
