+<a id="relation-to-known-results"></a>
+## Relation to known results
+
+**In words.** None of the ten central results is new mathematics. Each is near-definitional (it unfolds the theory's definitions in a few steps) or a known result restated in the theory's vocabulary, and the table names the closest prior result for each. What is the work's own is the artefact: one model in which every premise is named and witnessed both ways, the ethics with scope and order apart, and one vocabulary across conservation, selection and comparison. The verdicts are from an AI review that read every Lean statement against the literature it knew ([significance and prior-art review](·), 20 October 2026); the search was not exhaustive, and an earlier statement found later lowers a row.
