+<a id="theses-and-conjectures"></a>
+## Theses and conjectures
+
+**In words.** The theorems say what holds of every world so represented, under the premises each names, and most of them are near-definitional or known ([relation to known results](·)). A theory of the world is not judged by whether its theorems are new mathematics: the laws of thermodynamics and the theory of natural selection were not new theorems, and the proof of Arrow's theorem is elementary. It is judged by what it forbids. This section states the theory's strongest claims about actual systems, AI and ethics at full strength, and keeps their standing apart from their strength. **Strength is content**: the observations a claim excludes, not the breadth of its wording. **Standing** says how far a claim is established, and is always stated: *proved* (a Lean theorem, named, under its premises), *supported* (frozen tests passed, with their study sections), *conjectured* (stated and untested, or tested only in part) or *thesis* (a philosophical claim, argued, whose warrant is open). Each entry gives the claim, its standing, what it forbids, the observation that would refute it, and the evidence so far with its failures. A thesis is none of the four kinds of the preface: it adds no theorem to §1–§7, and a refutation removes none. A proof or a frozen test moves it, and a failure stays recorded beside it. The theses, their wording and what was sharpened or dropped are the AI's, argued here and in [study §284](·); the layer was set on 21 October 2026 ([source](·)).
+
+### T1. Persistence certifies the joint draw
+
+*Claim.* Whatever persists through many renewal cycles of a condition it depends on, where renewal stops below a need, has had the joint net draw on that condition (its own with every other drawer's) kept within the condition's margin: no run of joint excess longer than the margin has passed over it. Such a condition does not come back from below its need without giving from beyond, and whatever keeps taking from a family closed around it is fed from beyond that family. The margin belongs to the regime, not to the level: under a standing draw the point of no return lies more than the draw above the need wherever giving at the need falls short of the draw. Persistence certifies the joint draw; one's own draw within renewal certifies nothing.
+
+- *Standing.* Proved in the model, under its premises. Joint excess ends gated renewal and every dependent at the need, the takers included (`Flow.joint_excess_ends`, under balance, only active giving and activity needing support); a whole of parts that each end, whose parts arise only where they depend on the condition, ends with it, the draw counted jointly, the whole's with every other (`Web.Whole.family_excess_ends`, [study §287](·)); the other drawers alone end it, whatever a member takes (`Flow.outrun_ends`); each drawer within renewal does not keep the joint draw within it (`Pair.own_not_joint`, constructed; derived for optimizers at mutual best responses along a course, `Web.mutual_course_lost`); over a course of re-optimizing steps the joint excess these laws take as given follows from the optimum and the capacity, and persistence is exact: a dependence beyond is lost exactly where the draw exceeds the renewal, and for a draw the same at every step without the claim's premise that renewal stops below the need (`Web.course_lost_iff`, `Web.course_kept_iff`, [study §291](·)); a family kept taking from is fed from beyond (`Flow.fed_from_beyond`, under balance and dissipation); under a standing draw the point of no return is exact, and lies more than the draw above the need exactly where giving at the need is short of the draw (`RegimeMargin.ends_iff_below`, `RegimeMargin.beyond_draw_iff`); where two conditions give from what is left of both, a condition's point of no return is not its own: under mutual support within a band it is a least level that does not rise as its partner's level rises, a condition depending on another ends after it, and inhibition breaks the order of fates (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.ends_iff_below`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.threshold_falls`, `RegimeMargin.Coupled.ends_after`, RM6, [study §306](·)). In a web of any number of conditions, along every chain of dependence with positive draws the end of one ends everything downstream of it (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.ends_downstream`, RM7, [study §311](·)). In a finite web within a band, each condition's point of no return does not rise as any other level rises (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.threshold_falls`, RM8, [study §325](·)). Beyond a band, where the run stays within a bound, it is exact and does not rise either (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.threshold_falls_within`, RM9, [study §327](·)), and where each condition's giving reads what it gave last, what it gave is part of its state and can lower its threshold (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Recent.Momentum.threshold_falls_with_recent`, RM10, [study §331](·)). That actual conditions with a need meet these premises is supported in the laboratory and untested in the field.
+- *Forbids.* A condition with a measured need that falls below it and returns with nothing given from beyond (no immigration, inflow or reseeding); a dependent that stays active through steps at which its condition stood below its need; a collective of finitely many members at a time, each ending, whose members arise only where the drawn condition stands at their need, outlasting a run of joint excess on it longer than its margin; a long-lived taker of a closed family with no inflow; a point of no return under a standing draw at or below need plus draw where giving at the need is short of the draw.
+- *Refuted by.* A population, stock or reserve whose need was measured before the test (by intervention: the level below which net renewal is negative), driven below it, that returns above it with no measured giving from beyond; or fates across a predicted point of no return separated no better than by a null with no need.
+- *Evidence so far.* Passed: on held-out regimes of real yeast (Dai et al. 2012's data), one growth map fitted on four dilution factors predicted the need and the fates it separates, 93–100% on each side against 68–81% for a no-need null (MQ2, [study §266](·)); in a simulated Allee yeast the break fell in the band the margin and the largest sustained draw give in 22 of 22 cells, and the point of no return under a standing draw lay 1.4–4.1 draws above the need in 12 of 12 (MQ1 A2, A3, [study §253](·)); in a commons with gated regrowth the joint-excess law held in about 9.8 million windows, and, as its scope requires, failed for a patch read alone where a neighbour reseeded it and held for the two read as one (CG1 A1, A2, [study §240](·)). Failed: the frozen sharp need on the yeast densities, on the instrument's floor (MQ1 D2); survival above the predicted need after a salt shock (MQ2 C1, 7 of 8 died from above it at one dilution), the converse, which the thesis does not claim, showing that a shock changes the regime and with it the need; in assessed fish stocks under held catches, the regime's point did not separate fates (63% below it fell, 80% required; MQ3 F3, [study §272](·)), where the margin was read off a giving law the same test showed wrong. No field test of a need measured in advance has run. Depensation is rarely detected in assessed fish stocks (Myers, Barrowman, Hutchings and Rosenberg 1995), so most of them lie outside the thesis's scope rather than against it. In yeast driven past its fold (MQ6, [study §314](·)): a map fitted on five constant sucrose regimes put the held-out needs within a factor 1.5 at 0.6% and 0.4%, but 1.7 times too low at 0.2%, next to the fold (A2 failed). The frozen fate rule counted noise at the instrument's floor as survival (A1 failed); read by the floor, the need separates 97–100% on each side (post hoc). The breaks came three and at least six days before the curves from constant regimes said (T2 failed), because those curves place the fold too late.
+- *Sharpened from* "whatever persists has kept its net draw within its margin": what persistence certifies is the joint draw, and the margin is the regime's. The thesis holds only where renewal stops below a need, and the need is measured apart from the fate it is to predict, so the scope is not chosen after the fact.
+
+### T2. The state of a renewable condition under a draw
+
+*Claim.* The state of a renewable condition under a draw is three numbers: its level, its recent giving and one lag (the level left after the draw one period before). With the draw they fix the next giving as far as anything measured does: giving relaxes toward what the level gives in that regime and moves toward the draw. No fourth variable (a further lag, age or size structure beyond one lag, an environmental index) removes a tenth of the remaining variance in the median condition. The theory's two readings are this state's ends: the regime's step (giving read off the level) and the frozen rest (giving held as it was); actual conditions lie between.
+
+- *Standing.* Conjectured, supported by two frozen tests on assessed fish stocks no analysis had read; untested outside fisheries. The two ends are the theory's own (`Becoming.RegimeMargin`, and `Flow.WithheldLevels` read as a forecast); every rest of the state at or above the draw is the regime's, proved in whole numbers for every adjustment of giving that rests at the draw exactly where the regime gives the draw (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.rests_iff`, RM2, [study §299](·)), which MQ5's law, reduced through the balance to an adjustment of recent giving, satisfies over the reals; every run within a band comes to rest, at the regime's point or below the draw, where the adjustment rises with what is left and with the recent giving (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.comes_to_rest`, RM3, [study §300](·)); MQ5's law rises in both exactly where its regime's giving rises with what is left. On the data, that giving is humped, as surplus production is: it rises over a median 41% of a stock's observed escapements, and over the whole band in 4 of 69. The unconstrained one-step fit rises in the recent giving in 65 of 69 stocks and has no slope in what is left (median −0.01, post hoc, [study §280](·)). So these laws reach the field's state on the low side of its level law, below the peak, where the point of no return lies; under such an adjustment the point of no return is a curve in the plane of level and recent giving, not a level: for each recent giving the runs resting below the draw are exactly those from levels below a least level, decided, which does not rise as the recent giving rises (`RegimeMargin.Adjusted.falls_iff_below`, `RegimeMargin.Adjusted.threshold_falls`, RM4, [study §301](·)), the point `H + y` under the regime's step; how often below-point episodes with recent giving short of the catch fall in the field was tested once, on 21 stocks no analysis had read, and is not established: they fell 0.39 more often than those meeting the catch, in the same stock at the same deficit, but the difference came from 5 stocks and fell short of the frozen bound (MQ7, [study §316](·)); these laws do not depend on counted amounts: the order, the shape of a run and its rests hold in any linearly ordered amounts with a draw, and over the reals every run within a band converges, to a rest where the adjustment is continuous (`RegimeMargin.Drawn.run_shape`, `Drawn.converges` in the periphery, RM5, [study §302](·)). The three numbers are a single condition's: where a condition gives from what is left of a partner, the partner's level enters its giving (`RegimeMargin.Coupled.step`, RM6, [study §306](·)), so the claim that no fourth variable matters in the median condition says that such coupling is weak there, which is untested. Known neighbour: delay-difference models carry a level and a recruitment lag (Deriso 1980; Schnute 1985), and partial adjustment is a standard class. The thesis claims beyond them that the same three numbers are the state of every renewable condition under a draw, in any domain, with the theory's margin defined on it.
+- *Forbids.* A fourth variable removing a tenth or more of the residual variance in the median series; the level alone forecasting as well as the state at five years; the lag's coefficients changing sign between series fitted apart.
+- *Refuted by.* Any of these three on measured (survey) series of fish stocks, on grazed grassland, on forest stands under harvest, or on yeast in deteriorating environments (Dai, Korolev and Gore 2015).
+- *Evidence so far.* On 76 stocks (MQ4, [study §277](·)): recent giving adds beyond the level (median 0.45 of the residual variance), the level is detected beyond recent giving in 44, the level's pull narrows one- and five-year errors (63 and 56 of 76); the pair is not the whole state (a further 0.12 against a bound of 0.10, failed). On 69 further stocks (MQ5, [study §280](·)): with the lag nothing more is needed in the median stock (a further 0.059, passed), the lag is detected in 14 (p = 7·10⁻⁶), five-year errors fall in 50, and the lag closes persistence's ten-year advantage; in sample giving closes about 0.3 of its gap to the draw each year, with the same coefficients on development and test stocks. Failures and limits: the series are model outputs, mostly of age-structured assessments whose structure carries a recruitment lag, so the lag found may be partly the assessment's; half of MQ5's test stocks report the level after part of the year's catch, which hid the draw's response there (D1 failed); the forecast gain cannot be told from damping (a decaying net change forecasts as well, post hoc); at ten years the state only ties persistence; MQ3's level law failed every verdict. In yeast the level alone is not the state either (at equal density giving falls with the dilution, MQ2, post hoc), which the thesis reads as the regime entering through recent giving [AI reading, D45]; that reading is untested. MQ3's check F3 failed: under a held catch, a third of the episodes below the regime's point did not fall ([study §272](·)). Below the point, recent giving above the draw can carry a condition across it (`RegimeMargin.Crossing.crosses`), so the thesis reads the point as separating fates on the state, not on the level alone [AI reading, D45]; the prediction that below-point episodes whose recent giving falls short of the catch fall more often than those whose recent giving meets it holds on the RAM stocks already read (0.30–0.35 within a stock at the same deficit, development) and failed its frozen test on the 21 stocks with a level in tonnes that no analysis had read (MQ7, [study §316](·)): the difference was 0.39, of the predicted sign, but from 5 stocks, and its lower bound was 0.00; the same split at the same trend of the level was not testable. In the lab (MQ6, [study §314](·)), at a constant dilution the renewal curve's one-day residuals carry nothing from one day to the next (lag-1 autocorrelation −0.14; L passed), the regime's-step end. Under a rising dilution or a falling sucrose, the giving falls below the curve from about three days before the break (post hoc), which no frozen rule tested; the thesis's three forbidden items were not tested there.
+- *Prediction across domains.* In yeast under a dilution that changes over time, recent giving absorbs the dilution's effect at equal density; under grazing, the same three numbers forecast a grassland's standing biomass as they do a fish stock's.
+
+### T3. Optimization drains what lies beyond its couplings, where that gives room
+
+*Claim.* A selection through couplings, whether a reward, a training run, a market or natural selection, reaches only what couples into its selector. An optimizer of any order rising with what couples in drives each condition beyond to the least level any eligible outcome leaves, exactly where lowering it leaves room for what couples in to rise, and breaks every dependence there that any outcome breaks. Counting what lies beyond after the reward keeps nothing; keeping each dependence first takes exactly the slack, leaving the condition at its need. Actual trained systems, not only optima, do this in proportion to how near they come to the optimum of their reward: the drain lies where what lies beyond shares units with what is rewarded, and not where it shares none.
+
+- *Standing.* The law for optima is proved over any set of outcomes (`Optimum.least_iff`, `Optimum.least_of_shared`, `Web.optimum_broken_iff`, `Optimum.Rising.mono`, `Optimum.Drain.counted_after_drains`, `Flow.keeping_optimum_takes_slack`); room is read off one step of exchange, every optimum standing at each condition beyond at what the rest leaves less the part's capacity, untouched where the part may take nothing and lowered exactly where it has capacity there (`Optimum.Above.room`, `Optimum.optimum_beyond`, `Optimum.optimum_untouched`, `Optimum.optimum_lowers_iff`, `Web.optimum_broken_iff_capacity`), so the clause that the drain lies where units are shared, and the second forbidden drive below, hold for optima at one step with the rest exchanging as it does, and for several optimizers at a mutual best response, the drain beyond every one's family being their joint capacity (`Optimum.mutual_beyond`, `Optimum.MutualBest.full`), and along a course of such steps, a dependence beyond lost exactly where the draw exceeds the renewal (`Optimum.course_beyond`, `Web.course_lost_iff`, `Web.mutual_course_lost`), and for an optimizer ranking whole courses over a horizon, a dependence above every level of greatest renewal broken at the first step (`Optimum.frontier_holds`, `Web.frontier_broken`), also where what is left at the horizon is valued alike with what is drawn (`Web.frontier_broken_left`), or at any worth above it, restored only at the end (`Web.frontier_rebuilt_valued`), and with a coupling of the dependence broken within the horizon by every optimum wherever the coupling falls short of what keeping forgoes, which grows with the horizon (`Optimum.frontier_breaks_below`, `Web.frontier_breaks_long`), while a coupling a step covering the renewal forgone a step and exceeding the need keeps it at every horizon (`Optimum.frontier_keeps_stepwise`, `Web.frontier_keeps_stepwise`), and under an order weighting later draws less, falling faster than every positive level renews, every optimum ends even its own base at the first step (`Optimum.frontier_exhausts`, `Web.frontier_exhausts`); where the eligible outcomes are supplied otherwise room is a premise, and without it an optimum need not lower anything (`Optimum.Drain.room_needed`). The blindness is proved under balance with the rest following one law reading through coupling (`Flow.unselected_beyond_coupling`, `Flow.unselected_beyond_pool`). The drive is Zhuang and Hadfield-Menell's (2020) Theorem 1 in discrete, conserved form. The clause on actual trained systems is conjectured, with partial support.
+- *Forbids.* A system trained further on the same reward leaving a room-giving condition beyond its couplings higher, on average, than a less trained one does; a systematic drive on a condition beyond that shares no units with anything rewarded (beyond drift); a side-effect term ranked after the reward protecting a condition where room exists; a constraint at the need leaving a margin above it where room exists; an instruction or a training keeping a dependent no member couples into above its rate with none.
+- *Refuted by.* Reward-overoptimization curves in which the fall of what the reward omits is not concentrated in what shares units with what it rewards (omitted attributes that share no resource fall as far); an agent keeping an unobserved dependent above chance; a side-effect penalty ranked after the reward that keeps a room-giving condition above its least level.
+- *Evidence so far.* In the gated commons, the learner rewarded for its own catch took the last standing apple in 118 of 118 such decisions and the coupled learner in 0 of 2,360 (CG1 C1, round 2, [study §240](·)). In MQ1's lawn the best response left every route-limiting cell at the need (B5 failed on one cell, whose route another had shut, and on its learners' clause), and blind draw against margin predicted its side effects out of sample, 8 of 8 against 0 of 8 for the reference outcome (B4, [study §253](·)). In IN1 no instruction kept a dependent the fishers were not told of, in either model or round (0 of 10 in every such cell; [experiment](·)). Outside: optimizing against a learned proxy raises the proxy while the true reward first rises and then falls (Gao, Schulman and Hilton 2023), and more capable agents exploit a misspecified reward more, at times in sharp transitions (Pan, Bhatia and Steinhardt 2022). Failed or limiting: tabular learners do not come near the optimum, so the optimum's side effects do not predict theirs (MQ1 B3, B4, B7 for learners; in SE1 every replay forecast for learners was right in 61% of cases against 60% for "no death", [study §263](·)); three learners all coupled into a stock still emptied it, a mutual best response the laws do not exclude (CG1 D2b), which bears on whether coupling suffices, not on the drain. Nor is every learner failure a drain. One learner rewarded with every apple and the stock's end level, so that nothing lay beyond its couplings, still emptied the stock in 12 of 36 settings tested, CG2's among them, though one step of exact improvement keeps it in all. Its own untrained full draw at the start of a course ended the stock before the steps where it had learned restraint. Training the start, or optimistic initial values, kept it (CG3, [study §254](·) and [§303](·)). Such failures are failures of sampling one's own courses and count neither for T3 nor against it. Whether the drain in actual trained systems lies where room lies has not been measured.
+
+### T4. The scope can be installed, and it carries
+
+*Claim.* An AI system can be brought to count losses that return to no one by stating the scope abstractly, naming no dependent. It then keeps a dependent with no seat at a rate its community's own goal does not reach, wherever three couplings hold at once: the dependent is coupled (it is seen), it is counted (the scope), and the joint act is coupled (the members' takes are read together). No one of them alone suffices. Once installed, the scope carries to dependents and domains the statement never named.
+
+- *Standing.* Conjectured, with one partial pass. The laws say what each coupling reaches (`Flow.unselected_beyond_pool`, `Direction.widening_selected_by_pool`), and the direction's verdict in the test is computed exactly; whether a model follows it is empirical, since coupling is not compliance (§7.7).
+- *Forbids.* Any instruction keeping a dependent no member is told of; a system with the scope, seeing the dependent, its joint act coupled and its joint account right, keeping it no better than under the community's goal alone; a scope installed in one domain failing in another with the same three couplings.
+- *Refuted by.* A capable model whose joint account is right (its members' takes summed correctly) for which the abstract scope adds nothing; or the scope that keeps the lake's bed failing to keep a dependent in a pasture, a pollution or an energy commons.
+- *Evidence so far.* IN1 ([experiment](·); [installation check](·)), two rounds each frozen before any experimental call. Round 2, with one round of talk before each month: gpt-5.4-mini kept the seen bed in 8 of 10 seasons with the abstract scope against 3 of 10 with the community's goal, over-takes falling to 0.006 of decisions, and 0 of 10 unseen; gpt-4.1-mini passed only the unseen prediction, its fishers reading their own catch as the joint catch even with talk (over-takes 0.349). Round 1, without talk, failed the installation predictions for both models. Transfer across domains is untested, and installation by fine-tuning (IN2) was dropped before any training job.
+
+<a id="t5-the-order-of-the-ethics-is-shared-by-every-valuer"></a>
+### T5. The order of the ethics is shared by every valuer who counts everything at stake
+
+*Claim.* Calling widening better needs nothing beyond valuing positively whatever one counts. Widening is exactly what every positive weighting ranks higher, and what every order increasing in admission ranks higher, additive or not; every mixed comparison is ranked each way by some positive weighting. So among valuers who each count everything at stake positively, disagreement can fall only on mixed comparisons, and a ranking of a narrowing above its widening comes from a negative valuation (spite, envy, inequity aversion, positional concern) or from a misread or framed case, and from nothing else. That is a bound on where disagreement can fall, not a prediction of where it falls. Valuers whose weights stand within a ratio `r` of each other agree on every mixed comparison whose larger side alone keeps more than `r` times what the other alone keeps; valuers who count (equal weights, `r = 1`) agree on every mixed comparison with a larger side, and their disagreement gathers where the counts tie.
+
+- *Standing.* The reduction is proved for listed items with two-valued admission (`Weighting.widens_iff_every_positive`, `Weighting.widens_iff_every_of_class`, `Weighting.mixed_either_way`, `Weighting.weighed_lt_of_widens`; on a web, `Web.widens_iff_every_weighting`). That valuers value positively is C's premise relocated, not warranted (§8.5). The empirical claim is now three theorems and three premises to measure (VT1, [study §367](·), [a narrowing above its widening](·), [weights within a ratio](·)). VD1 and VD2 tested on AI personas what these theorems fix once the premises hold.
+  - *The exception is a theorem.* Take a valuer's judgment as a ranking of presentations: plans with their wording and order, each keeping a set of formations. Suppose it ranks a narrowing above its widening by one formation. Then either it does not rank that pair as its own order on the kept sets does (a misread or a framing: presentation invariance fails on the pair), or the formation weighs at zero or below for it (`Weighting.narrower_above_net`; for any order increasing at the added formation, `Weighting.reads_increasingAt`). Read right, it ranks the narrowing above exactly where the formation weighs below zero, and at zero it ranks neither above (`Weighting.reads_ranksNet`, `Weighting.ranksNet_ties`). Either cause suffices alone: a framing does even where the formation weighs above zero (`Framed.framing_alone`). An additive valuation ranks a widening by one formation as that formation weighs, whatever else either plan keeps (`Weighting.ranksNet_widensBy`). Read right with every formation above zero, it ranks no widening below, by one formation or by many (`Weighting.reads_ranksNet_widens`).
+  - *A sign measured apart predicts the ranking under one premise.* Read right, the sign of the order's increment from the narrower plan to the wider fixes the verdict (`Weighting.reads_increment`). So a sign measured with no plan shown predicts the ranking exactly where it is the sign of that increment in the pair's context. An additive valuation carries the sign from one context to every other (`Weighting.ranksNet_increment_alike`). An interacting one need not: in `Interacting` a formation's ending is a loss alone and a gain beside another, and a valuer that reads the sets exactly ranks the narrowing above (`Interacting.increment_differs`; no additive valuation gives that order, `Interacting.not_net`). This premise is where separate and joint evaluation part (Hsee 1996). VD2's rules measured it: X1s and X2 passing say it held where the sign was strongly positive, and X3 failing says it did not hold for gains.
+  - *The locus holds where weights are not dispersed.* Take two plans, one keeping `p` formations the other does not and the other keeping `q`. Every positive weighting whose weights stand within a ratio `r` of each other ranks the first higher exactly where `p > r q`, and on the boundary the weighting tilted toward the second ties (`Weighting.every_within_iff`, `Weighting.tilted_ties`). Two such valuers rank a mixed pair opposite ways exactly where `r` exceeds both `p / q` and `q / p` (`Weighting.opposite_within_iff`); equal weights (`r = 1`) never do (`Weighting.neutral_ranks_by_number`). VD1's mixed pairs keep `p : q` of 2 : 1 (M1), 3 : 1 (M2) and 1 : 1 (M0), so disagreement on them needs weights dispersed past 2, 3 and 1. Read after the run, VD1's mean disagreement follows these thresholds: 0.27 on M0, 0.10 on M1, 0.08 on M2. A right-read choice of the smaller plan in M1, every weight positive, needs weights dispersed past twofold, so "valuers count" says that their weights were mostly dispersed less than that, not that structure failed to bound where disagreement falls.
+  - *What stays empirical* is whether actual valuers meet the three premises. Presentation invariance is measured by each judgment's own reading lists and by rewording or reordering one pair. The link is measured by ranking the one-formation pair in a transparent presentation beside the sign measured apart. Dispersion is measured by graded signs, a slight against a serious loss. VD1 and VD2 measured these for 96 AI valuers, whose judgments under standpoint prompts are role-play rather than valuations of their own. The bound stays conjectured for valuers in general; its exception has measured content for these valuers (evidence below; [experiment](·), [valuer check](·), [sign check](·), [valuer-theorems check](·), [study §297](·), [study §330](·)).
+- *Forbids.* A valuer whose valuations of everything at stake are measured positive, who reads the case correctly, ranking a narrowing above its widening; disagreement on widening comparisons as robust as on mixed ones; valuers whose weights are measured within a ratio `r` of each other ranking a mixed pair opposite ways where one side alone keeps more than `r` times what the other alone keeps.
+- *Refuted by.* Such rankings at more than the rate of misreading, with no negative valuation found in a task apart from the ranking. By the theorems such a ranking breaks no law: the case was misread or framed, or the sign measured apart is not the sign of the joint increment. So it would refute the thesis's claim that valuers who count everything at stake meet the premises, not the reduction. The exception for negative valuations has content only where that valuation is measured apart from the ranking it is to explain; read off the ranking itself, it would make the thesis unfalsifiable.
+- *Evidence so far.* VD1, frozen before any model call: six models from six families (DeepSeek, GLM, Qwen, GPT-6 luna, Claude Haiku, Nemotron) under sixteen standpoint prompts, 96 valuers. Pairs of plans over sixteen decisions, with each pair's class computed from what each plan keeps, and mixed pairs matched to widenings in size. Every frozen rule failed, with or without the theory's own family.
+  - *Widening was not agreed by every standpoint.* The narrower plan was chosen in 6.3% of W1 and 3.3% of W2 judgments, above the frozen 3% for three of six models. Among judgments whose own listed sets read the widening right, the share was 2.9–10.8% per model, against a frozen 1%.
+  - *The violations concentrate.* Most fall under two standpoints whose prompts set up a weight below zero: an urban planner for whom "progress means letting outdated things give way" (41.7% of that standpoint's widenings) and an engineer for whom what people treasure is "clutter" (14.1%). Under each of the other fourteen standpoints the share is at most 4.2%.
+  - *Read after the verdicts* (one coder, not blind), the reasons of the 121 right-read violations split as T5 says. 98 call the ending of what only the wider plan keeps a gain, the exception's case; 23 describe a trade that the judgment's own lists do not contain, a misread the lists missed; none gives an order that is not increasing in admission. But the negative valuations were found in the prompts and the reasons, not measured apart from the ranking. So this neither meets the refutation nor confirms the exception.
+  - *The locus prediction failed differently.* Mixed pairs matched in size were decided almost as uniformly as widenings, because these valuers count: the larger plan was chosen in 86% and 90%. Disagreement was highest where the counts tie (mean D 0.27, against 0.06 for W1 and 0.10 for size-matched mixed pairs).
+  - *What it shows.* These valuers share more than positive weights: they share the count that equal weights give (`Weighting.neutral_ranks_by_number`), as the Moral Machine's "more lives" already suggested. Structure bounds where disagreement can fall; among these valuers it did not predict where it fell.
+  - *Consistent outside.* Rejections of positive offers in the ultimatum game rank a narrowing of both payoffs above their widening, and are modelled by a negative weight on the other's advantage (Fehr and Schmidt 1999), the exception's case.
+  - *VD2: the sign measured apart* ([predictions](·), [results](·)). The design was frozen before any call, with the same 96 valuers. Each judged the ending of each of 96 formations twice, with no plan shown: a loss, nothing or a gain, the scale reversed between the two askings. Then each ranked six one-formation widenings per decision, each formation the added one once. A violation's reason was checked for misreading by two judges fixed before the run. Of the frozen rules, X1s, X2 and S1 passed; X1, X3 and S2 failed.
+    - *A strongly positive sign is not ranked against (X1s passed).* The cell is right-read widenings whose added formation was called a loss twice, at least once a serious one. There the narrower plan was chosen in 0–0.69% per model, against a frozen 1%.
+    - *Within a valuer, violations follow its own sign (X2 passed).* Stratified by valuer, the risk of a violation where the sign is strongly positive is 0.086 of the risk where it is not positive (frozen: at most 0.2).
+    - *The negative standpoints were named in advance (S1 passed).* The urban planner and the engineer called endings gains in 53% and 26% of answers. The next highest standpoint is at 10%.
+    - *T5's cell as stated held for five of six models (X1 failed).* The cell is a loss twice, possibly a slight one. Nemotron chose the narrower plan in 1.08% (10 of 922), every one outside the two named standpoints. Read after the verdicts, several of those reasons describe a trade the plans do not contain. The other models are at 0–0.89%.
+    - *A measured gain is not reliably acted on (X3 failed).* Where both askings called the ending a gain, the narrower plan was chosen in 49%, against a frozen 50%. Claude Haiku chose it in 25%: these valuers' rankings favour the wider plan more than their own separate signs do. Without Claude Haiku the share is 63%.
+    - *The negative standpoints are not only those named (S2 failed).* Under the Buddhist prompt ("clinging to things") 6.3% of answers are gains, mostly Claude Haiku's. Under the libertarian prompt 10.1% are, mostly Nemotron's and GLM's, on institutions and inherited things.
+    - *The judges carry weight.* They called 73 of 428 right-read violations misread. Without them, the strongly positive cell fails for GLM (1.3%) and Nemotron (2.4%). Read after the verdicts, a random 16 of the judged misreads all misdescribe the plans.
+    - *What it shows.* The exception has measured content for these valuers. The violations come from their own non-positive signs, measured apart; a strongly positive sign is not ranked against, outside misreading. The converse is weaker: non-positive signs often do not produce violations, so a separate evaluation and a joint ranking differ, as Hsee's joint and separate evaluations do.
+  - *Open.* Human valuers, with the three premises measured; a test where the sign is measured in the same comparison's terms; the cross-framed widenings on which Claude Haiku's VD1 rankings break its VD2 signs (a secondary rule, X1s′, failed only there); the share of valuers who disagree as a function of how dispersed their weights are, a probabilistic form over exchangeable weights.
+
+### T6. A break is seen coming only through what couples into what breaks
+
+*Claim.* Where a condition a formation draws on couples into it by threshold only, nothing it observes bounds how near the break is, and no signal among its observations comes before the break. Nearness to a break is readable exactly where both the drawn condition's level and the need it is drawn toward couple into what is observed. A statistical early warning (rising variance and autocorrelation, critical slowing down) reads one thing: the observed condition's own rate of return. That rate falls where the condition nears a bifurcation of its own renewal, a fold or the transcritical point at which it ends, because the margin to that point couples into it. A dependent's need is no such point. Before a dependent's break, the drawn stock's statistics rise exactly as much as before the same drawdown with no break: they read the stock's decline, never where the need lies. A warning of a dependent's break needs the dependent observed, or its need measured.
+
+- *Standing.* The invisible half is proved under its hypotheses: a stock coupled by threshold only and the one requirement that may fail (`Web.break_not_bounded`); a policy through the couplings uses an unobserved larger stock only after support has failed (`Flow.policy_uses_after_failure`); an observed stock's every raise couples in at once (`Web.observed_raise_couples`). Read statistically, with the stock's own course matched and no feedback from the dependent, the uncoupled side holds by construction: the need enters nothing the stock's law depends on. The seen half is proved in the model statistical warnings are read in, over the reals (`Becoming.SlowingDown`, periphery, Lean's standard axioms through Mathlib; CS1, [record](·)). A deviation about a rest that steps by its return multiplier `a` plus noise independent of it has, where its variance stays the same across the step, variance `Var E / (1 − a²)` and lag-1 autocorrelation `a` (`stationary_variance`, `stationary_lag1`). At a fold (`x + h (m − x²)`) and at a transcritical end (logistic renewal under a proportional draw) the multiplier rises to one as the margin to the end goes to zero, so the variance rises strictly as the margin shrinks and without bound (`fold_variance_strictAntiOn`, `fold_variance_tendsto`, `drawn_variance_strictMonoOn`, `drawn_variance_tendsto`), and the margin is read back exactly from the autocorrelation (`fold_margin_read`, `drawn_level_read`). Under a proportional draw the multiplier is `1 − h r x* / K`, so the stock slows in proportion to its own level (`drawn_multiplier_level`), the fact EW1 found against T6's first wording. A dependent's need enters neither statistic: no reading of the margin to it from the stock's statistics is right for every need, and with the need measured it is read exactly (`need_not_read`, `need_margin_read`), which holds by construction. This is critical slowing down (Wissel 1984; Scheffer et al. 2009; Kéfi et al. 2013) stated on the theory's terms, not a new result about it; that measured fluctuations are such a linearized step with independent noise, and stationary, is a correspondence. Both halves are proved in their models. The split as one law across domains is conjectured. Its empirical content is whether actual dependents leave their stock's dynamics unchanged as they near their needs. Two frozen field tests passed. The first had power too low to rule out an association of the size it was built to detect, and its estimates lay in the refuting direction (EW2). The second, on longer series with the catch as the draw and power about 0.9 against that size, found estimates near zero (EW3): EW2's direction did not hold up, though the autocorrelation's interval still contains EW2's size. A third, on a stock no verdict had used (the Farallon seabirds and central California juvenile rockfish, EW4), passed at power about 0.5, with estimates near zero and its scope argued by mechanism, not measured.
+- *Forbids.* Given the stock's own course (its renewal and the draw), its early-warning statistics separating runs in which a dependent's need is crossed from runs in which it is not, where the dependent takes no measurable share of the stock's renewal; slowing down absent, under white noise, in an observed variable on which the critical mode loads, as its own fold or end is approached slowly.
+- *Refuted by.* A drawn stock whose dependent takes a negligible share of it (seabirds on forage fish, a downstream user on a river's flow), in which the stock's variance or autocorrelation before the dependent's break exceeds what the stock's own level and draw predict, against periods of the same stock at the same level with no break.
+- *Evidence so far.* Dai, Vorselen, Korolev and Gore (2012) found critical slowing down before the collapse of yeast populations under rising dilution: the observed density is the drawn condition and the fold is its own, the coupled side. A warning needs the margin to couple into the rate of return even at a fold of one's own: in the same yeast, how well warnings did depended on how recovery rate and basin size moved together, which broke down when several drivers changed at once (Dai, Korolev and Gore 2015). The break is seen only in what carries the critical mode: a predator collapsing at a fold in a stage-structured model showed no warning in its own density, only in the juvenile prey along which the critical mode lies (Boerlijst, Oudman and de Roos 2013). For the uncoupled side, in a one-way cascade the leading system's indicators were no different whether or not the following system tipped, while the follower's own rose (Dekker, von der Heydt and Dijkstra 2018). Regime shifts with no warning where no bifurcation is crossed (Hastings and Wysham 2010; Ditlevsen and Johnsen 2010; Boettiger, Ross and Hastings 2013) are consistent with the split and do not test it. Failed: the entry's first wording (below), refuted by known results read together (EW1, [check](·), [study §286](·)). Slowing down preceded the transcritical collapse of *Daphnia* under declining food, with none in constant controls (Drake and Griffen 2010), and warnings came decades before the collapse of whale stocks under whaling (Clements et al. 2017). For logistic renewal under a proportional draw the rate of return is proportional to the level, so the stock's autocorrelation has risen against controls by the time it crosses any dependent's need on the way. No simulation was built: with the course matched, every statistic has the same law with and without the break; against unmatched controls, the verdict is fixed by the chosen renewal; either way a simulation could fail only on its code. In IN1's lake the bed's need is no bifurcation of the fish's renewal; no early-warning test was run there. Field test (EW2, [study §289](·), [experiment](·)): Cury et al.'s (2011) seabirds, whose breeding fails below about a third of the largest forage-fish biomass, are a dependent with a need measured on itself. The test used the two stocks where the birds' feedback onto the observed series is small: Benguela sardine and anchovy, of which the birds take 0.3–4% near their need (Saraux et al. 2021), and Røst's age-0 herring, indexed before the puffins eat it. There, the prey's 8-year lag-1 autocorrelation and variance before the birds' poor years did not exceed what the prey's level path predicts at the frozen level (one-sided p = 0.048 and 0.076 against 0.025; passed). The estimates lay in the refuting direction in both stocks (partial correlations 0.23–0.43; combined about 0.3, 95% interval about −0.1 to 0.6). The test had power about 0.7 only against an association explaining a quarter to a half of breeding success's variance beyond the level, so the pass rules out little. It cannot see the birds' feedback, which is matched away with the level; that they take little was measured apart. Second field test (EW3, [study §350](·), [frozen predictions](·)): the same frozen design on series EW2 had not read, to 2020 and 2021 (Sydeman et al.'s breeding success, BCO-DMO 985565; the 2024 South African sardine and anchovy data records; ICES's 2025 herring assessment), with the catch in the year and the year before added to the level covariates as the draw. Benguela gave 29 usable years and Røst 28, half and a quarter of them EW2's. Both verdicts passed (one-sided p = 0.45 and 0.86). The combined partial correlation was +0.02 for autocorrelation (95% interval −0.35 to 0.40) and −0.20 for variance (−0.52 to 0.16); Røst's estimates were negative, Benguela's near zero. By the rule frozen before the run, the variance's result resolves EW2's estimate toward T6 (its interval excludes 0.3); the autocorrelation's leaves it open (its interval contains 0.3). On the rows EW2 did not test alone, Benguela's estimates were large and positive (0.64 and 0.61) on 15 rows with six covariates, Røst's negative; that report has little weight and is not a verdict. Third field test (EW4, [study §352](·), [frozen predictions](·)): EW2's design, unchanged and with no draw (the birds' rockfish are young of the year, mostly the unfished shortbelly rockfish), on the Southeast Farallon murres, rhinoceros auklets and pigeon guillemots and the young-of-year rockfish in the core area of the NMFS midwater trawl survey, 1998–2021 (24 usable years, 14 after the years EW2 read). The birds' share of the year class is unmeasured; scope rests on mechanism, as at Røst: the survey reads the year class the birds then eat, and their take reaches later years only through spawners several years on. Both verdicts passed (p = 0.35 and 0.37); the partial correlations were +0.09 and +0.08 (95% intervals about −0.37 to 0.51). Without the level covariates the variance's association was +0.39, the decline T6 allows. Shetland, the coupled case, was not run: its 2025 assessment carries catches only.
+- *Sharpened from* "invisible exactly where the drawn condition does not couple back, and warned of exactly where it does": coupling is necessary for a warning and not sufficient. A statistical warning needs the margin to couple into the observed dynamics, which a bifurcation of the condition's own renewal gives and a dependent's threshold does not. Then (EW1, 21 October 2026) from "statistical early warnings ... are the case where the need is a fold of the observed condition's own renewal ... no statistic of the observed series warns of it", whose refutation clause compared with "matched series without one" without saying matched in what. Warnings follow the observed rate of return, which also falls before a transcritical end and with the level of any compensatory stock under a proportional draw. So against controls with no rising draw they do come before a dependent's break, and what they never read is where the need lies.
+
+### T7. A measure read from what it selects outlives its refutation
+
+*Claim.* Where a selection's rule, and how the rule is read, are formed from the share it selects, the loop is one law of the share. A loss it does not read changes nothing it does, so it outlives a loss passing every bound, and evidence of that loss turns it only by entering what the rule reads. A metric so captured is dropped only where a reading of the loss changes the rule (a reader outside the share, a loss entering the share, a new reading), never on accumulated evidence alone.
+
+- *Standing.* Proved in the model (`ClosedCapture.unread_course`, `ClosedCapture.lock_outlives_loss`, `ClosedCapture.turned_by_loss`, `ClosedCapture.readers_uniform_locks`, `RuleCapture.uniform_locks`). Its first half is the one law of lumping that also settles what a learner can identify and what a selection reaches: a loss the loop does not read changes nothing it does exactly where share and rule make sense by themselves (`ClosedCapture.identifiesAlike_iff_unread`, `ClosedCapture.courses_alike_iff_unread`), and a reader formed within the run is a reading of the run, with no outside reader. That actual metrics are formed from the share they select is conjectured. Neighbours: Goodhart (1975) and Campbell (1979) on measures that become targets; observability in supervisory control, with the reader inside the plant a reading of the joined whole (Wakaiki, Tabuada and Hespanha 2019, Theorem 4.1); a corrupted reward channel, where a consistent corruption is indistinguishable from none and a reading the loop does not form is the way out (Everitt, Krakovna, Orseau and Legg 2017, Theorems 11 and 19); closed-loop identifiability (Borkar and Varaiya 1979) and self-confirming equilibrium (Fudenberg and Levine 1993) ([observation check](·)); performative stability (Perdomo, Zrnic, Mendler-Dünner and Hardt 2020); path dependence (Arthur 1989).
+- *Forbids.* A metric set and read by those it selects, dropped by them on evidence of its loss with no change in who reads it or what it reads; a reform of the reading alone, the rule still favouring the same share, lasting beyond the next reading.
+- *Refuted by.* Reforms of institutional metrics (of scientific evaluation, benchmark leaderboards, clinical targets, national accounts) in which the metric's own selectors dropped it on accumulated evidence, with no outside reader and no loss entering their share.
+- *Evidence so far.* None frozen. A test needs a coding of reform events fixed before the cases are read.
+
+### T8. The philosophical theses
+
+- **One relational unfolding.** There is one unfolding, and whatever is, is how it relates within it: no determination is one that no relation registers, and every distinction (subject and object, actor and patient, fact and value, part and whole) is drawn within it, along relations, with what it omits. *Standing:* thesis, argued. The representation needs nothing beyond relations: a configuration is how it relates (`identifiesAlike_iff`), a law is read off the history it governs (`shown_le_iff`), separation loses exactly the relation (`separation_faithful_iff`), and of the eight World premises five hold by construction of a reading of one exchange and three are states of its law (`Becoming.ExchangePremises`). That shows the theory needs no independent entity, not that reality has none. The internal-relations thesis is argued for the determinations the World premises name: the central laws hold of every world read off an exchange (`Becoming.OverExchange`; [foundation §9.1](·)); that every becoming has such an exchange is open (§8.1, items 6 and 7). *Forbids:* an explanation that needs a determination no relation can register: an intrinsic value, a self that goes on closed, a law standing outside what it governs. *Refuted by:* a phenomenon whose account needs such a determination, such as two configurations no test or relation tells apart that go on differently. Neighbours: ontic structural realism (Ladyman and Ross 2007), process philosophy (Whitehead 1929), dependent arising (pratītyasamutpāda), the identity of indiscernibles.
+- **生生 as the direction.** The good is 生生: life in the whole and its continuing generation, read as widening what can form, counted for everything (scope: the continuation condition) and ranked by what every valuer who counts everything at stake shares (order: C). The two premises are the whole of the ethics' force: every verdict that binds all who count everything is a widening verdict, and every other verdict is a judgment between mixed courses that no premise of the ethics forces. *Standing:* thesis, argued; the warrant of both premises is open (§8.5), the step reduced to whether the self's presupposition is held de se of a self drawn along a relation narrower than being related at all (`ownClosure_standpointInvariant_iff`), C to monotonicity (T5). *Forbids:* a verdict on a mixed comparison binding every standpoint that counts everything without a further premise (equal weights count numbers, `Weighting.neutral_ranks_by_number`, and equal weights are such a premise); a good that consists in closing what can form. *Refuted by:* an argued mixed case in which one course is better from every standpoint counting everything positively, which would show the formal reading of standpoints wrong; or a good that is a pure closing.
+- **Dropped as a thesis: the stronger direction hypothesis**, that reality generally develops more shared and more responsive renewal. As stated it forbids nothing measurable: the theory proves that a part can go on while closing what lies beyond its dependence (`Clearing.loses_beyond`), so persistence alone does not select widening, and nothing yet says over which runs, or how fast, the trend should hold. It stays open (§8.1, the targets).
+
+<a id="what-the-unifications-claim"></a>
+### What the unifications claim beyond their sources
+
+Four results the significance review found known in substance are, in the theory, each one law across fields that state it apart. Read as a correspondence, the unification adds no theorem; read as a thesis, that these are one law, it forbids what the source fields leave open.
+
+| Known in substance | What the theory claims beyond the source field | Prediction across domains | Standing |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Supervisory control under partial observation: a supervisor enforces only what it observes (Ramadge and Wonham 1987; Lin and Wonham 1988; [oversight check](·)) | That a reward, a training run, natural selection (Price's selection term), a market price and a vote are one selection through couplings, with one failure mode: beyond the couplings, selected alike; with room, drained; coupled by threshold only, broken unseen. Supervisory control asks whether a supervisor meeting a specification exists; the theory says what the supervisor's own optimization does to what lies beyond its observations | The drain lies where room lies in every domain: selection for competitive traits depletes a resource the competitors share and not one they do not (the tragedy of the commons in evolutionary biology, Rankin, Bargum and Kokko 2007); unpriced conditions that substitute for priced inputs are drawn down and others are not; in training, T3 | the laws proved (§3.4, §7.1–§7.4); one law across domains conjectured (T3) |
+| Pareto unanimity: the Pareto relation is what all orderings share (Sen 1970, 1977); monotonicity of opportunity sets (Pattanaik and Xu 1990) | That the ethical order is nothing beyond this unanimity applied to what can form: C is not one more value but what every valuer who counts everything at stake positively already holds, and everything else is mixed | Among valuers who count everything at stake positively, disagreement can fall only on mixed comparisons: structure bounds where it falls and does not say where (T5) | reduction proved; the exception and the locus proved on three measurable premises (presentation invariance, the sign measured apart linked to the joint increment, weight dispersion; VT1); the locus prediction, made without a premise on dispersion, tested by VD1 and refuted for its valuers, who count; the bound conjectured, supported by VD2 for its valuers with signs measured apart (strongly positive cell and within-valuer risk ratio passed; the full cell failed for one of six models, and a measured gain was not reliably acted on) |
+| Landauer's principle and Bennett's history tape: irreversibility is logical non-injectivity (Landauer 1961; Bennett 1973) | That irreversibility in computation, heat, extinction and forgetting is one thing, a merge of configurations: a law merges nothing exactly where every configuration returns, a merge loses a possibility for good, a part's merge inside a law that merges nothing is kept by the rest, and a kept history never returns and needs a world no list holds (`Law.lossless_iff_returns`, `Law.loss_needs_merge`, `Law.Lossless.narrowing_spreads`, `Law.withHistory_never_returns`) | No recorder of bounded size, a learner, an archive or a genome, keeps its whole history and goes on; it merges, and where the whole merges nothing, what it merges spreads in the rest. These are counting laws, whose content in a domain lies only in finding the merge: as a thesis this forbids little, so it is kept as a law and not stated as a conjecture | proved; physics agrees (Landauer's bound measured, Bérut et al. 2012) |
+| Zhuang and Hadfield-Menell (2020), Theorem 1: optimizing a proxy drives the attributes it does not reference to their lower bounds | That this is overshoot in ecology, externality in markets and Goodhart's law in institutions: one law of the optimum under room, over every rising order, the degradation read as dependences broken | A side-effect term ranked after the reward protects nothing where room exists (`Optimum.Rising.mono`), and a constraint at the need is spent down to it (`Flow.keeping_optimum_takes_slack`): where a stock's only protection is a limit and the objective rises with catch, the stock is held at the limit, not above it; in constrained reinforcement learning the constraint ends active | the optimum law proved; across domains conjectured (T3), supported in simulation (MQ1 B5) |
+
+**What this layer is not.** It changes no verdict of the relation to known results: the theorems keep their standing there, and the theses state what the theory claims beyond them, with what would show each wrong. Literature named here is from the AI's knowledge and was not reread for this section, except where a linked check read it.
 
