+### 8.9 Objections not yet answered
+
+Each stands against the account as stated, with what would answer it. Where one is answered, answered in part or sharpened into an exact question, the entry says which and links the argument; none is shown to defeat the step, and the step is not shown.
+
+- **The step across standpoints (Gewirth's critics).** From "I must value my continuation" nothing follows about another's; universalizing yields only that each standpoint holds its own to matter. It hits the step across standpoints, which from each standpoint's own presupposition forces exactly the centers (`forced_iff_center`), and not the step across drawings (`boundaryInvariant_iff_all`); the half aimed at rights has no target, since the theory makes no claim of right or duty. *Sharpened* ([THE-STEP-OF-INVARIANCE §6.1](·), [§4.1](·)). The egoist reply is exactly the de se reading of the presupposition. Held de se, as a property each standpoint ascribes to itself, the presupposition gives each center its own closure, invariant only where the centers' closures agree (`ownClosure_standpointInvariant_iff`). Held de dicto, the step forces the union of closures (`forced_iff_within_some`). The two readings agree exactly where the closures agree (`selfAscribed_iff_withinSome`), and along being related at all in a connected unfolding the de se reading is the condition with no step (`ownClosure_unrestricted_of_whole`). So the de se objection and the privileged-relation objection are one, and the exact open question is this: is the self's presupposition held de se of a self drawn along a privileged relation narrower than being related at all? *Would answer it:* an argument either way on that question.
+- **Agent-relative reasons and partiality.** Williams argued that agent-relative reasons and partial attachments are not defects awaiting universalization (“one thought too many”). *Answered for two-valued significance* ([§6.2 there](·)): the step fixes scope only; partial choices (one's wife or a stranger) are mixed comparisons, which C does not rank and every weighting counting everything may decide either way (`Weighting.mixed_either_way`), so there is no impartial verdict for partiality to be licensed against; partiality cannot rank a widened course above its widening (`Weighting.weighed_lt_of_widens`) or count a loss as nothing (`Weighting.weighed_eq_of_unweighted`). The price is that C also leaves the grossest partiality unranked where numbers differ (Taurek's position). *Answered for graded significance too* (IV2): the step gives standing (whether a formation counts), not status (how much). Invariant grades give invariant standing and rank alike from every standpoint (`Weighting.ranks_alike_of_gradeInvariant`), but invariant standing does not give invariant grades (`Partial.ranks_differ`). Numbers count (`Weighting.neutral_ranks_by_number`) only under the further premise that status is invariant and equal, which the theory does not assert. *What remains:* an argument for or against that premise.
+- **Why “anything” has significance**, a hurricane or a tumour included. *Sharpened* ([§6.3 there](·)). The narrower scope, what wants its continuation read as the centers of standpoints [AI reading, D59], is checked: retaining under it is admitting every center (`Web.retains_atCenters_iff`), and it parts from the condition exactly at a formation that is no center (`Clearing.centers_retain_yet_loses`). The tumour does not tell the scopes apart (on the conatus reading of wanting it is a center, and ending it is mixed on both); the hurricane does only on a reading of wanting stronger than conatus. “Anything” is not idle: it decides which losses C counts. *Would answer it:* an argument for which formations hold standpoints, and for covering, every formation within some standpoint's closure along a relation the unfolding reads; covering by feeding is the defensible part.
+- **The externalism of A.** Internalists deny a reason where no motive or sound deliberation connects to it. *Sharpened* ([§6.4 there](·)): restated internally, from a standpoint's presupposition along the relations its concern carries, a reason reaches exactly the closure (`forced_iff_within`), and everything route (b) proves survives (§6.3, `Flow.Balances.presupposed_reach_comparison`); A's external part is exactly the step. *Would answer it:* a sound deliberative route from the presupposition to invariance, or an argument that there is none.
+- **Graded status, priority and constraints.** *Answered* for graded status, priority, sufficiency and constraints against closing ([§6.5 there](·)).
+  - Graded status is a positive weighting. It agrees with C wherever C ranks and decides only mixed comparisons (`Weighting.weighed_lt_of_widens`, `Weighting.mixed_either_way`). Status zero is a boundary (`Weighting.weighed_eq_of_unweighted`).
+  - Priority on levels of continuation (steps admitted, `Weighting.level`), IV2: a strictly increasing transform agrees with C wherever C ranks (`Weighting.prior_lt_of_widens`, Pareto). A transform strictly concave up to a bound decides one-step transfers that C leaves mixed (`Weighting.prior_transfer`, Pigou–Dalton).
+  - Sufficiency is a scope denial above its threshold (`Weighting.sufficient_ties`).
+  - Lexical priority is no additive weighting.
+  - A constraint against closing never conflicts with C (`Web.not_widens_of_closes`).
+
+  *Sharpened* for constraints on acts rather than outcomes (doing and allowing beyond closing, promising). *Would answer it:* whether such a constraint reads as a de se ranking of outcomes (Howard 2022), and so decides only mixed comparisons. Well-being beyond the length of continuation is not modelled.
+- **Which function is learned.** The laws of §7.1–§7.4 hold for every selection through the couplings and say nothing about which function training installs, inductive bias, goal misgeneralization or deception. *Would answer it:* results on which law a trained system's acts come to follow, joined to the learning laws, and evidence for identified installations.
+- **The internal-relations thesis.** *Answered in part* ([foundation §9.1](·)): within the representation, the determinations the World premises name are readings of one exchange, four of their ties hold by what the readings are, and every central law then holds of every world read off an exchange (`Becoming.OverExchange`). *Would answer the rest:* that every becoming has a law or relation of exchange whose readings these are (items 6 and 7), and an argument that requiring does not read the current level of what is required, which with `ExchangeRelation.respondsBelow_weakest` makes requirement necessary response ([foundation §9.1](·)).
+- **Every review so far is by AI.** *Would answer it:* independent human review of the Lean statements against the prose and of the philosophical arguments, beginning with §6 and §7.
 
